const STORIES = [
{id:'a1-lost-key',season:{id:'riverside-season-1',episode:1,name:'The Riverside Club'},title:'The Lost Key',level:'A1',tone:'#F3C86A',emoji:'🔑',minutes:3,decision:{afterPage:1,prompt:'You cannot find your key. What is the best next step?',prompt_ar:'لا تستطيع العثور على مفتاحك. ما أفضل خطوة تالية؟',options:[{text:'Look carefully in the places where you last used it.',text_ar:'ابحث بعناية في الأماكن التي استخدمت المفتاح فيها آخر مرة.',response:'Good strategy: checking likely places first is calm and practical. In the story, Mia searches her bag and under the chair before following her dog.',response_ar:'استراتيجية جيدة: ابدأ بتفقد الأماكن المحتملة بهدوء وبطريقة عملية. في القصة، تبحث ميا في حقيبتها وتحت الكرسي قبل أن تتبع كلبها.',branchPage:['🔎','Mia checks the garden path carefully and spots a tiny muddy footprint beside the flower bed.','تبحث ميا بعناية في ممر الحديقة وتلاحظ أثرًا صغيرًا قرب حوض الزهور.'],endingPage:['🔎','Mia returns the key to its hook by the door. The next morning, she remembers her careful search and feels ready to solve small problems.','تعيد ميا المفتاح إلى مكانه قرب الباب. وفي الصباح التالي، تتذكر كيف ساعدها البحث الهادئ على حل المشكلة.']},{text:'Give up and leave the door unlocked.',text_ar:'التخلي عن البحث وترك الباب دون قفل.',response:'This might seem faster, but it does not solve the problem safely. Keep looking and ask for help if needed.',response_ar:'قد يبدو هذا أسرع، لكنه لا يحل المشكلة بأمان. واصل البحث واطلب المساعدة عند الحاجة.',branchPage:['🚪','Mia asks her neighbour to stay with her while she checks the door and calls her family for help.','تطلب ميا من جارتها البقاء معها، ثم تتصل بعائلتها طلبًا للمساعدة.'],endingPage:['🚪','With help, Mia gets safely inside later. She learns that asking for help is better than leaving the home unsecured.','تدخل ميا المنزل بأمان لاحقًا بمساعدة الآخرين. وتتعلم أن طلب المساعدة أفضل من ترك المنزل دون تأمين.']},{text:'Blame someone before checking.',text_ar:'إلقاء اللوم على شخص قبل التحقق.',response:'Blaming without evidence can upset people and still leave the key missing. Look for clues first.',response_ar:'إلقاء اللوم دون دليل قد يزعج الآخرين، ولن يعيد المفتاح. ابحث عن دلائل أولًا.',branchPage:['🗣️','Mia pauses, apologises, and asks everyone to help retrace their steps instead of arguing.','تتوقف ميا وتعتذر، ثم تطلب من الجميع البحث معًا بدلًا من الجدال.'],endingPage:['🗣️','They find the key near the garden flower. Mia learns that calm questions solve problems faster than blame.','يعثرون على المفتاح قرب الزهرة. وتتعلم ميا أن الأسئلة الهادئة تحل المشكلات أسرع من اللوم.']}]},pages:[['🏠','Mia is at home. She cannot find her key. Mia takes a slow breath and thinks about the last time she used the key. She remembers opening the garden gate after school. Her bag is heavy, so she puts it on the table and checks each pocket carefully. She wants to solve the problem without making a mess.','ميا في المنزل. لا تستطيع العثور على مفتاحها. تأخذ ميا نفسًا هادئًا وتتذكر آخر مرة استخدمت فيها المفتاح. تتذكر أنها فتحت بوابة الحديقة بعد المدرسة. تضع حقيبتها الثقيلة على الطاولة وتتفقد جيوبها واحدًا واحدًا. تريد حل المشكلة دون إحداث فوضى.'],['🧥','She looks in her bag and under the chair. The key is not there. She asks her family if anyone has seen it, but nobody remembers. Instead of becoming angry, Mia looks at the floor and checks the places near the door. Her mother suggests retracing her steps. Mia learns that a small plan can make a confusing problem easier.','تنظر في حقيبتها وتحت الكرسي. المفتاح ليس هناك. تسأل ميا أفراد عائلتها إن كان أحد قد رأى المفتاح، لكن لا أحد يتذكر. بدلًا من الغضب، تتفقد الأرض والأماكن القريبة من الباب. تقترح أمها تتبع خطواتها السابقة. تتعلم ميا أن خطة بسيطة تجعل المشكلة المحيرة أسهل.'],['🐶','Her little dog runs to the garden. Mia follows him and sees a shiny key near a flower. The dog waits beside the flower bed and wags his tail. Mia notices a small mark in the soft soil, then sees the key shining between two leaves. She picks it up carefully and thanks her dog. Now she knows that looking closely can reveal a useful clue.','يركض كلبها إلى الحديقة. تتبعه ميا وترى مفتاحًا لامعًا قرب زهرة. ينتظر الكلب قرب حوض الزهور ويحرك ذيله. تلاحظ ميا أثرًا صغيرًا في التراب الناعم، ثم ترى المفتاح يلمع بين ورقتين. تلتقطه بحذر وتشكر كلبها. وتعرف الآن أن النظر بعناية قد يكشف دليلًا مفيدًا.'],['😊','Mia picks up the key and opens the door. “Good dog!” she says. Before going inside, Mia cleans the key and puts it on a hook beside the door. She tells her family what happened and shows them the muddy mark. Everyone smiles at the little dog. Mia decides to put important things in the same place every day. She feels ready for tomorrow. Later, Mia pins a note about the Riverside Club weekend garden day on the community board. Sam and Lina promise to bring food, while Nora offers to welcome new neighbours.','تلتقط ميا المفتاح وتفتح الباب. تقول: كلب جيد! قبل الدخول، تنظف ميا المفتاح وتعلقه في مكان قرب الباب. تخبر عائلتها بما حدث وتريهم الأثر الطيني. يبتسم الجميع للكلب الصغير. وتقرر ميا أن تضع الأشياء المهمة في المكان نفسه كل يوم. لاحقًا، تعلق ميا إعلانًا عن يوم الحديقة لنادي ريفرسايد على لوحة الحي. يعد سام ولينا بإحضار الطعام، وتعرض نورا الترحيب بالجيران الجدد.']],vocab:{key:['a small piece of metal used to open a lock','مفتاح','kee','I use my key to open the door.'],find:['to discover where something is','يعثر على','fynd','Can you find my bag?'],garden:['an area outside where plants grow','حديقة','GAR-dən','We play in the garden.'],shiny:['bright because light reflects from it','لامع','SHY-nee','The shiny coin is new.']},questions:[['Where does Mia find the key?',['In the garden','In her bag','Under the chair'],0,'The dog leads Mia to the garden, where she sees the key.'],['What does “shiny” mean here?',['Reflecting light','Very old','Very soft'],0,'The key reflects light, so it looks shiny.'],['Who helps Mia find the key?',['Her dog','Her sister','Her teacher'],0,'Mia follows her little dog to the garden.']]},
{id:'a1-rainy-picnic',season:{id:'riverside-season-1',episode:2,name:'The Riverside Club'},title:'A Rainy Picnic',level:'A1',tone:'#91C9E8',emoji:'🧺',minutes:3,decision:{afterPage:1,prompt:'The rain starts during your picnic. What would you do?',prompt_ar:'بدأ المطر أثناء نزهتك. ماذا ستفعل؟',options:[{text:'Pack the food and find a safe, dry place.',text_ar:'اجمع الطعام وابحث عن مكان آمن وجاف.',response:'A practical choice. It protects the food and helps everyone stay comfortable, just like Sam and his sister do.',response_ar:'اختيار عملي؛ فهو يحمي الطعام ويساعد الجميع على الشعور بالراحة، كما فعل سام وأخته.',branchPage:['☕','Sam packs the food in a bag and leads his sister to the nearby café before the rain gets heavier.','يضع سام الطعام في الحقيبة ويقود أخته إلى المقهى قبل أن يشتد المطر.'],endingPage:['☕','They enjoy a warm indoor picnic and plan to check the weather before their next outdoor trip.','يستمتعان بنزهة دافئة داخل المقهى ويقرران التحقق من الطقس قبل النزهة القادمة.']},{text:'Stay outside and ignore the weather.',text_ar:'ابقَ في الخارج وتجاهل الطقس.',response:'That could leave everyone cold and wet. Checking the weather and moving somewhere safe is wiser.',response_ar:'قد يجعل ذلك الجميع يشعرون بالبرد والبلل. من الأفضل متابعة الطقس والانتقال إلى مكان آمن.',branchPage:['🌧️','The rain grows heavier, so Sam and his sister quickly move under the café awning and ask to sit inside.','يزداد المطر، فينتقل سام وأخته سريعًا إلى مكان جاف قرب المقهى.'],endingPage:['🌧️','They dry off and share the food indoors. Sam realises that changing a plan can still save a good day.','يجففان ملابسهما ويتقاسمان الطعام في الداخل. يدرك سام أن تغيير الخطة قد ينقذ اليوم.']},{text:'Throw the picnic away immediately.',text_ar:'تخلّص من طعام النزهة فورًا.',response:'That is unnecessary. The food can still be enjoyed somewhere dry.',response_ar:'لا داعي لذلك؛ يمكن الاستمتاع بالطعام في مكان جاف.',branchPage:['🧺','Sam protects the food in the bag, then looks around for a dry place rather than throwing anything away.','يحمي سام الطعام في الحقيبة ويبحث عن مكان جاف بدلًا من رميه.'],endingPage:['🧺','They find a warm café nearby and enjoy the picnic after all. A small adjustment saves their plans.','يعثران على مقهى دافئ ويستمتعان بالنزهة في النهاية. تعديل بسيط أنقذ خطتهما.']}]},pages:[['🌳','Sam and his sister pack a picnic. They take apples, bread, and juice to the park. Sam checks the basket one more time while his sister, Lina, carries a small blanket. They have planned the picnic since Monday. Their mother reminds them to take a light jacket, but the morning sun makes the park look warm and bright.','يحضر سام وأخته نزهة ويأخذان التفاح والخبز والعصير إلى الحديقة. يتفقد سام السلة مرة أخرى بينما تحمل أخته لينا بطانية صغيرة. لقد خططا للنزهة منذ يوم الاثنين. تذكرهما أمهما بأخذ سترة خفيفة، لكن شمس الصباح تجعل الحديقة تبدو دافئة ومشرقة.'],['☁️','They sit under a tree. Dark clouds cover the sky, and cold rain begins to fall. At first, the park is busy with children and families. Sam and Lina choose a tree with a wide trunk and sit on the grass. They open the basket and begin to eat. Then the wind moves the leaves, and the sky slowly turns grey.','يجلسان تحت شجرة. تغطي الغيوم الداكنة السماء ويبدأ المطر بالهطول. في البداية، تكون الحديقة مزدحمة بالأطفال والعائلات. يختار سام ولينا شجرة ذات جذع عريض ويجلسان على العشب. يفتحان السلة ويبدآن الطعام. ثم تحرك الرياح الأوراق وتتحول السماء ببطء إلى اللون الرمادي.'],['🏃','Sam puts the food in the bag. They run to a small café near the park. A few large drops fall on the blanket. Lina protects the bread while Sam closes the basket. They do not run into the road or leave their things behind. They walk quickly along the path and look for a place where they can stay dry.','يضع سام الطعام في الحقيبة ويركضان إلى مقهى صغير قرب الحديقة. تسقط قطرات كبيرة على البطانية. تحمي لينا الخبز بينما يغلق سام السلة. لا يركضان إلى الطريق ولا يتركان أغراضهما. يسيران بسرعة على الممر ويبحثان عن مكان يبقيهما جافين.'],['☕','The café is warm and dry. They share their picnic and laugh about the rain. Inside the café, the owner gives them two napkins and points to a table near the window. They dry their hands and arrange the food again. The rain becomes a silver curtain outside, but their day is still enjoyable. They decide that a good plan can change. Sam draws a tiny sun on the basket. At the Riverside Club, Mia arrives with her dog while Nora helps Lina choose a dry place for the next meeting. The group decides to keep a weather plan with every picnic invitation.','المقهى دافئ وجاف. يتقاسمان طعام النزهة ويضحكان على المطر. داخل المقهى، يعطيهما صاحبه منديلين ويشير إلى طاولة قرب النافذة. يجففان أيديهما ويرتبان الطعام من جديد. يصبح المطر ستارًا فضيًا في الخارج، لكن يومهما يظل ممتعًا. ويقرران أن الخطة الجيدة يمكن تغييرها. في نادي ريفرسايد، تصل ميا مع كلبها بينما تساعد نورا لينا في اختيار مكان جاف للاجتماع القادم. وتقرر المجموعة إرفاق خطة للطقس بكل دعوة إلى نزهة.']],vocab:{pack:['to put things into a bag for a trip','يحزم','pak','Pack your books before school.'],cloud:['a white or grey shape in the sky','سحابة','klowd','A dark cloud is over the house.'],share:['to use or enjoy something together','يتقاسم','shair','We share our lunch.'],dry:['not wet','جاف','dry','My coat is dry now.']},questions:[['Why do they leave the tree?',['It starts to rain','They are hungry','It is too hot'],0,'Cold rain begins to fall, so they move to the café.'],['What does “dry” mean?',['Not wet','Very cold','Full of food'],0,'They are safe from the rain inside the café.'],['What do they do in the café?',['Share their food','Buy a tree','Go swimming'],0,'They eat the picnic together and laugh.']]},
{id:'a2-night-train',season:{id:'riverside-season-1',episode:3,name:'The Riverside Club'},title:'The Night Train',level:'A2',tone:'#A99BEA',emoji:'🚆',minutes:4,decision:{afterPage:1,prompt:'A stranger has lost a suitcase at the station. How can you help?',prompt_ar:'فقد شخص غريب حقيبة سفر في المحطة. كيف يمكنك مساعدته؟',options:[{text:'Ask where they last saw it and help check nearby places.',text_ar:'اسأل أين رآها آخر مرة وساعده في تفقد الأماكن القريبة.',response:'This is helpful and focused: gather a useful detail, then check likely locations together.',response_ar:'هذا تصرف مفيد ومحدد: اجمع معلومة مهمة ثم تفقدوا الأماكن المحتملة معًا.',branchPage:['🧳','You ask the traveller to describe the suitcase and check the bench where they last sat.','تطلب من المسافر وصف الحقيبة وتتفقد المقعد الذي جلس عليه آخر مرة.'],endingPage:['🧳','A station worker spots the suitcase near the bench. The traveller thanks you, and you both make the train with time to spare.','يعثر موظف المحطة على الحقيبة قرب المقعد. يشكرك المسافر وتلحقان بالقطار في الوقت المناسب.']},{text:'Take their word for it and leave the station alone.',text_ar:'صدّقه ثم غادر المحطة وحدك.',response:'You do not need to solve everything alone, but you can help them contact station staff and retrace their steps.',response_ar:'لست مضطرًا إلى حل كل شيء وحدك، لكن يمكنك مساعدته في التواصل مع موظفي المحطة وتتبع خطواته.',branchPage:['🧑‍✈️','You walk with the traveller to the station help desk and explain what happened.','ترافق المسافر إلى مكتب المحطة وتشرح للموظف ما حدث.'],endingPage:['🧑‍✈️','Staff check the lost-property area and locate the suitcase. The traveller learns where to report a problem next time.','يفحص الموظفون قسم المفقودات ويعثرون على الحقيبة. ويتعلم المسافر أين يبلّغ عن المشكلة لاحقًا.']},{text:'Open every suitcase you see.',text_ar:'افتح كل حقيبة تراها.',response:'That would invade other people’s privacy. Look for the described suitcase and ask station staff for help.',response_ar:'هذا ينتهك خصوصية الآخرين. ابحث عن الحقيبة الموصوفة واطلب مساعدة موظفي المحطة.',branchPage:['🛑','You stop before touching other bags and ask a station employee to help identify the missing suitcase.','تتوقف قبل لمس الحقائب الأخرى وتطلب مساعدة أحد موظفي المحطة.'],endingPage:['🛑','The employee finds the right bag using the traveller’s description. You help without disturbing anyone else’s belongings.','يعثر الموظف على الحقيبة الصحيحة من وصفها. وقد ساعدت دون العبث بممتلكات الآخرين.']}]},pages:[['🚉','Nora arrived at the station just before sunset. Her train was delayed, so she bought a warm drink. Nora had packed a book, a charger, and a small sandwich for the journey. She checked the departure board twice because the station was unfamiliar. Around her, people were talking quietly or watching the clock. She had plenty of time, so she tried to stay patient.','وصلت نورا إلى المحطة قبل الغروب. تأخر قطارها فاشترت مشروبًا دافئًا. وضعت نورا كتابًا وشاحنًا وشطيرة صغيرة في حقيبتها للرحلة. تفقدت لوحة المغادرة مرتين لأن المحطة لم تكن مألوفة لها. كان الناس حولها يتحدثون بهدوء أو يراقبون الساعة. كان لديها وقت كافٍ، فحاولت التحلي بالصبر.'],['🧳','While she was waiting, an older man asked whether she had seen a blue suitcase. He had left it near the ticket desk. The man looked worried and kept checking his pockets. He explained that the suitcase held clothes and a folder of important papers. Nora asked him to describe its colour and size before they searched. She knew that clear details would help them avoid taking someone else’s bag.','بينما كانت تنتظر، سألها رجل إن كانت قد رأت حقيبة زرقاء تركها قرب مكتب التذاكر. بدا الرجل قلقًا وظل يتفقد جيوبه. أوضح أن الحقيبة تحتوي على ملابس وملف أوراق مهمة. طلبت نورا منه وصف لونها وحجمها قبل البحث. وعرفت أن التفاصيل الواضحة ستساعدهما على تجنب أخذ حقيبة شخص آخر.'],['🔎','Nora remembered seeing the suitcase beside a bench. They hurried back and found it exactly where he had described. They returned to the bench and asked a station worker for help. The worker checked the nearby seats and the lost-property desk. Soon, a cleaner pointed toward the blue case beside a timetable stand. The man checked the label and smiled with relief.','تذكرت نورا الحقيبة بجانب مقعد. عادا بسرعة ووجداها في المكان الذي وصفه. عادا إلى المقعد وطلبا المساعدة من أحد موظفي المحطة. تفقد الموظف المقاعد القريبة ومكتب المفقودات. وبعد قليل، أشار عامل النظافة إلى الحقيبة الزرقاء قرب لوحة المواعيد. تحقق الرجل من البطاقة وابتسم بارتياح.'],['🌙','When the train finally arrived, the man thanked Nora. She boarded feeling glad that a small detail had helped someone. When Nora finally sat by the train window, she thought about how easily a journey can become stressful. A calm question and a little teamwork had solved the problem. She opened her book, listened to the wheels begin to move, and felt ready for the trip. The man later visits the Riverside Club and thanks Nora again. Mia introduces him to Sam, Leo, Daniel, and Amina, who are planning a small community open day together.','عندما وصل القطار، شكر الرجل نورا. صعدت سعيدة لأن تفصيلًا صغيرًا ساعد شخصًا. عندما جلست نورا أخيرًا قرب نافذة القطار، فكرت في سهولة تحول الرحلة إلى موقف متوتر. لقد حل سؤال هادئ وقليل من التعاون المشكلة. فتحت كتابها، واستمعت إلى صوت العجلات وهي تتحرك، وشعرت أنها مستعدة للرحلة. يزور الرجل نادي ريفرسايد لاحقًا ويشكر نورا مجددًا. وتعرّفه ميا إلى سام وليو ودانيال وأمينة، الذين يخططون معًا ليوم مفتوح صغير لأهل الحي.']],vocab:{delayed:['happening later than planned','متأخر','di-LAYD','Our flight was delayed.'],bench:['a long seat for several people','مقعد طويل','bench','We sat on a bench in the park.'],remember:['to bring something back into your mind','يتذكر','ri-MEM-ber','I remember your name.'],boarded:['got onto a train, bus, or plane','صعد إلى وسيلة نقل','BOR-did','They boarded the train at noon.']},questions:[['Why did Nora go back with the man?',['To look for his suitcase','To buy a ticket','To find a café'],0,'The man had left his blue suitcase near the station desk.'],['What does “delayed” mean?',['Later than expected','Very crowded','Already gone'],0,'Nora had to wait because the train did not arrive on time.'],['How did Nora feel at the end?',['Glad she had helped','Angry','Afraid'],0,'She felt good because remembering a detail helped someone.']]},
{id:'a2-bread-mystery',season:{id:'riverside-season-1',episode:4,name:'The Riverside Club'},title:'The Missing Bread',level:'A2',tone:'#E8A27F',emoji:'🍞',minutes:4,decision:{afterPage:1,prompt:'You suspect someone took the bread, but you have no proof. What would you do next?',prompt_ar:'تظن أن أحدًا أخذ الخبز، لكن ليس لديك دليل. ماذا ستفعل بعد ذلك؟',options:[{text:'Observe carefully and look for evidence before blaming anyone.',text_ar:'راقب بعناية وابحث عن دليل قبل لوم أي شخص.',response:'A fair choice. Evidence helps you solve the problem without hurting someone unfairly.',response_ar:'اختيار منصف؛ فالدليل يساعدك على حل المشكلة دون إيذاء شخص ظلمًا.',branchPage:['🔍','Leo decides to watch the kitchen quietly and notices a trail of flour near the counter.','يقرر ليو مراقبة المطبخ بهدوء ويلاحظ أثرًا من الدقيق قرب المنضدة.'],endingPage:['🤝','Leo apologises to Ben and they make a plan to keep the food safe. Their relationship becomes warmer because Leo admits his mistake.','يعتذر ليو لبن ويضعان خطة لحفظ الطعام. وتصبح علاقتهما أفضل لأن ليو اعترف بخطئه.']},{text:'Accuse your brother again so he confesses.',text_ar:'اتهم أخاك مجددًا حتى يعترف.',response:'Pressure may cause an argument, but it will not tell you what really happened.',response_ar:'قد يؤدي الضغط إلى جدال، لكنه لن يكشف ما حدث فعلًا.',branchPage:['😟','Ben becomes upset and leaves the kitchen. Leo notices that repeating an accusation has not answered the question.','ينزعج بن ويغادر المطبخ. ويلاحظ ليو أن تكرار الاتهام لم يجب عن السؤال.'],endingPage:['🧩','Leo calms down, asks Ben to help investigate, and discovers the cat is responsible. They agree to check facts before blaming each other.','يهدأ ليو ويطلب من بن مساعدته في البحث، فيكتشفان أن القط هو السبب. ويتفقان على التحقق قبل لوم أحدهما الآخر.']},{text:'Throw away all the food and stop investigating.',text_ar:'ارمِ الطعام كله وتوقف عن البحث.',response:'That wastes food and leaves the real problem unsolved. A simple check is more useful.',response_ar:'هذا يهدر الطعام ويترك المشكلة دون حل. سيكون التحقق البسيط أنفع.',branchPage:['🥖','Leo saves the food, closes the container, and asks his family for a better idea.','يحفظ ليو الطعام ويغلق الوعاء ويطلب من عائلته فكرة أفضل.'],endingPage:['🐈','The family discovers the cat has been stealing the bread and changes where it is stored. Leo learns to solve a problem instead of avoiding it.','تكتشف العائلة أن القط كان يأخذ الخبز وتغير مكان حفظه. ويتعلم ليو حل المشكلة بدل تجنبها.']}]},pages:[['🥪','Every morning, Leo found one slice of bread missing from the kitchen. He blamed his brother, who always denied taking it. Leo was sure that his brother Ben was taking the bread because Ben often ate late at night. Each morning, Leo asked him about it, and each morning Ben looked hurt. Their parents told them to stop arguing until they had a real answer.','كل صباح، كان ليو يجد شريحة خبز مفقودة. اتهم أخاه الذي كان ينكر أخذها. كان ليو متأكدًا أن أخاه بن يأخذ الخبز لأن بن كان يأكل غالبًا في وقت متأخر. كل صباح كان ليو يسأله، وكان بن يبدو منزعجًا. طلب منهما والداهما التوقف عن الجدال حتى يعثرا على إجابة حقيقية.'],['🕵️','On Saturday, Leo woke up early and hid behind the door. He waited quietly with a notebook in his hand. Leo made a small plan instead of asking the same question again. He put a fresh slice on a clean plate and left a little flour near the counter. Then he hid where he could see the kitchen without frightening anyone. The house became quiet as the clock moved toward six.','يوم السبت، استيقظ ليو مبكرًا واختبأ خلف الباب منتظرًا بهدوء. وضع ليو خطة صغيرة بدلًا من تكرار السؤال نفسه. وضع شريحة خبز طازجة في طبق نظيف وترك قليلًا من الدقيق قرب المنضدة. ثم اختبأ في مكان يرى منه المطبخ دون إخافة أحد. ساد الهدوء بينما اقتربت الساعة من السادسة.'],['🐈','At six, the cat jumped onto the counter and pulled the bread toward the floor. Leo had blamed the wrong person all week. The cat moved slowly at first, then jumped onto the counter with surprising confidence. It pulled the bread down and carried it toward its bowl. Leo nearly laughed, but he also felt embarrassed. The flour showed tiny paw marks, clear evidence of what had happened.','في السادسة، قفز القط إلى المنضدة وسحب الخبز. كان ليو يتهم الشخص الخطأ طوال الأسبوع. تحرك القط ببطء في البداية، ثم قفز إلى المنضدة بثقة مفاجئة. سحب الخبز وحمله نحو وعائه. كاد ليو يضحك، لكنه شعر بالحرج أيضًا. أظهر الدقيق آثار أقدام صغيرة، وكانت دليلًا واضحًا على ما حدث.'],['😹','Leo apologised to his brother. The next day, they put the bread in a closed box and gave the cat a toy instead. Leo told Ben the truth and apologised without making excuses. Together, they bought a container with a lid and moved the bread away from the edge. They also gave the cat a toy and fed it at the right time. The kitchen became peaceful again. At the Riverside Club, Leo tells Mia, Sam, Nora, Daniel, and Amina what the cat taught him about checking facts. They laugh, then volunteer to prepare snacks for the open day.','اعتذر ليو لأخيه. في اليوم التالي، وضعا الخبز في صندوق مغلق وأعطيا القط لعبة. أخبر ليو بن بالحقيقة واعتذر دون اختلاق الأعذار. اشتريا معًا وعاءً بغطاء وأبعدا الخبز عن الحافة. كما أعطيا القط لعبة وقدما له الطعام في الوقت المناسب. وعاد الهدوء إلى المطبخ. في نادي ريفرسايد، يخبر ليو ميا وسام ونورا ودانيال وأمينة بما تعلمه من القط عن التحقق من الحقائق. يضحكون ثم يتطوعون لإعداد وجبات خفيفة لليوم المفتوح.']],vocab:{missing:['not present where expected','مفقود','MIS-ing','One page is missing from my book.'],blamed:['said someone was responsible for a problem','لامَ','blaymd','She blamed me for the mess.'],quietly:['without making much noise','بهدوء','KWY-it-lee','Please walk quietly.'],apologised:['said you were sorry','اعتذر','uh-POL-uh-jyzd','He apologised for being late.']},questions:[['Who took the bread?',['The cat','Leo’s brother','A neighbour'],0,'Leo sees the cat pull the bread from the counter.'],['What does “blamed” mean?',['Said someone caused the problem','Gave a gift','Asked a question'],0,'Leo said his brother was responsible, but he was wrong.'],['What did Leo do after?',['Apologised to his brother','Bought more cats','Hid the notebook'],0,'He said sorry because he had accused his brother unfairly.']]},
{id:'b1-last-bus',season:{id:'riverside-season-1',episode:5,name:'The Riverside Club'},title:'The Last Bus',level:'B1',tone:'#75C7B0',emoji:'🚌',minutes:5,followUp:{taskId:'world-a2-on',label:'Practise the bridge in the village'},decision:{afterPage:1,prompt:'You may miss the last bus. Which response is most effective?',prompt_ar:'قد تفوتك الحافلة الأخيرة. أي تصرف هو الأكثر فاعلية؟',options:[{text:'Check the next stop and compare the safest route and timing.',text_ar:'تحقق من المحطة التالية وقارن بين الطريق الآمن والتوقيت.',response:'Good problem-solving: use the available information, consider timing, and choose a safe route rather than rushing blindly.',response_ar:'حل جيد للمشكلة: استخدم المعلومات المتاحة وراعِ الوقت واختر طريقًا آمنًا بدل التسرع دون تفكير.',branchPage:['🗺️','You check the timetable and take the well-lit path to the closer stop.','تراجع جدول الحافلات وتسلك الطريق المضاء إلى المحطة الأقرب.'],endingPage:['🗺️','You reach the stop safely and catch the last bus. You learn that a quick check can be more useful than a risky sprint.','تصل إلى المحطة بأمان وتلحق بآخر حافلة. كان التحقق السريع أنفع من الركض الخطر.']},{text:'Run across the road wherever it looks shortest.',text_ar:'اركض عبر الطريق حيثما بدا أقصر.',response:'Saving a few seconds is not worth risking your safety. Choose a safe route and crossing.',response_ar:'لا تستحق الثواني القليلة المخاطرة بسلامتك. اختر طريقًا ومعبرًا آمنين.',branchPage:['🚦','You stop at the crossing and use the safe route, even though it takes a little longer.','تنتظر عند ممر العبور وتسلك الطريق الآمن حتى لو استغرق وقتًا أطول.'],endingPage:['🚦','You miss that bus, but the driver at the next stop points you to a safe late service. Getting there safely mattered most.','تفوتك تلك الحافلة، لكن السائق يرشدك إلى خدمة متأخرة وآمنة. كانت سلامتك أهم.']},{text:'Assume there is no solution and stop trying.',text_ar:'افترض عدم وجود حل وتوقف عن المحاولة.',response:'It is easy to feel stuck, but checking nearby stops or asking someone for reliable advice may reveal an option.',response_ar:'من السهل الشعور بالجمود، لكن تفقد المحطات القريبة أو طلب نصيحة موثوقة قد يكشف خيارًا آخر.',branchPage:['📱','You call the transport information line and ask about another safe route home.','تتصل بخدمة معلومات النقل وتسأل عن طريق بديل وآمن للعودة.'],endingPage:['📱','You find a later connection and message your family with the updated plan. Asking for information turns a dead end into a solution.','تجد رحلة لاحقة وترسل لعائلتك خطتك الجديدة. حوّل طلب المعلومات طريقًا مسدودًا إلى حل.']}]},pages:[['🌆','By the time Daniel reached the stop, the last bus had already left. He was about to call a taxi when a cyclist slowed down beside him. Daniel had stayed late to help a colleague finish a difficult task. By the time he left the office, the streets were quieter and most shops had closed. He checked his phone and realised that he had misread the timetable. The final bus was already gone.','عندما وصل دانيال إلى الموقف، كان آخر حافلة قد غادرت. كان على وشك طلب سيارة أجرة حين أبطأت راكبة دراجة بجانبه. بقي دانيال في العمل حتى وقت متأخر لمساعدة زميل على إنهاء مهمة صعبة. وعندما غادر المكتب، كانت الشوارع أهدأ وأغلقت معظم المتاجر. تفقد هاتفه واكتشف أنه قرأ جدول المواعيد خطأ. كانت الحافلة الأخيرة قد غادرت بالفعل.'],['🚲','The cyclist recognised him from the neighbourhood. “If you take the road beside the river, you can catch the bus at the next stop,” she said. The cyclist did not simply tell him to hurry. She asked which direction he needed and checked the time on her own phone. Then she explained that another stop was closer if he followed the river road. Daniel thanked her and looked for the safest crossing.','تعرفت عليه راكبة الدراجة من الحي وأخبرته أنه يستطيع اللحاق بالحافلة عند الموقف التالي. لم تكتفِ راكبة الدراجة بأن تطلب منه الإسراع. سألته عن وجهته وتحققت من الوقت في هاتفها. ثم أوضحت أن محطة أخرى أقرب إذا اتبع طريق النهر. شكرها دانيال وبحث عن معبر آمن.'],['🌉','Although he was tired, Daniel followed her advice. He reached the next stop just as the bus was turning the corner. The river path was quiet, but the lamps were working and the pavement was clear. Daniel kept his phone away so he could watch the road. When he reached the corner, he saw the bus indicator glowing in the distance. He waved only after reaching the stop.','رغم تعبه، اتبع دانيال نصيحتها. وصل إلى الموقف بينما كانت الحافلة تنعطف. كان الطريق بجانب النهر هادئًا، لكن المصابيح كانت تعمل والرصف واضحًا. أبعد دانيال هاتفه كي ينتبه للطريق. وعندما وصل إلى الزاوية، رأى إشارة الحافلة تضيء من بعيد. لوّح للسائق بعد أن وصل إلى الموقف.'],['🙌','He made it with seconds to spare. The next morning, he thanked the cyclist and decided to leave home earlier from then on. On the bus, Daniel sent a short message to his family to say he was on his way. The next morning, he thanked the cyclist when he saw her near the shops. He also saved the timetable on his phone. One late evening had taught him to prepare better. At the Riverside Club, Daniel tells Mia, Sam, Nora, Leo, and Amina about the cyclist advice. The group adds safe travel details to its plan for the coming open day.','لحق بالحافلة قبل فوات الأوان بثوانٍ. في الصباح شكر راكبة الدراجة وقرر الخروج أبكر. في الحافلة، أرسل دانيال رسالة قصيرة لعائلته ليخبرهم أنه في طريق العودة. وفي الصباح التالي، شكر راكبة الدراجة عندما رآها قرب المتاجر. كما حفظ جدول المواعيد في هاتفه. علمته أمسية متأخرة أن يستعد بصورة أفضل. في نادي ريفرسايد، يخبر دانيال ميا وسام ونورا وليو وأمينة بنصيحة راكبة الدراجة. وتضيف المجموعة تفاصيل عن التنقل الآمن إلى خطة اليوم المفتوح القادم.']],vocab:{recognised:['knew who someone was from before','تعرّف على','REK-ug-nyzd','I recognised her voice.'],advice:['a suggestion about what someone should do','نصيحة','ad-VYSS','My teacher gave me useful advice.'],although:['despite the fact that','رغم أن','awl-THOH','Although it was late, we continued.'],spare:['extra time remaining','وقت إضافي','spair','We arrived with five minutes to spare.']},questions:[['Why did Daniel change his route?',['A cyclist suggested a faster way','The road was closed','He wanted a walk'],0,'The cyclist told him how to reach another stop in time.'],['What does “with seconds to spare” mean?',['Just before it was too late','After hours','Without a watch'],0,'Daniel arrived only moments before the bus turned away.'],['What did Daniel decide?',['Leave home earlier','Buy a bicycle','Move away'],0,'He wanted to avoid missing the bus again.']]},
{id:'b1-quiet-lab',season:{id:'riverside-season-1',episode:6,name:'The Riverside Club'},title:'The Quiet Lab',level:'B1',tone:'#8CB5E8',emoji:'🧪',minutes:5,decision:{afterPage:1,prompt:'The sensor gives strange readings again. What is the best next step?',prompt_ar:'يعطي المستشعر قراءات غريبة مجددًا. ما أفضل خطوة تالية؟',options:[{text:'Repeat a controlled test and record what changes.',text_ar:'أعد اختبارًا مضبوطًا وسجل ما يتغير.',response:'A controlled test helps separate evidence from guesses and makes the result easier to trust.',response_ar:'يساعد الاختبار المضبوط على فصل الأدلة عن التخمين ويجعل النتيجة أكثر موثوقية.',branchPage:['📋','Amina keeps the sensor in one place and changes only one condition at a time.','تبقي أمينة المستشعر في مكانه وتغير عاملًا واحدًا في كل مرة.'],endingPage:['💡','The team identifies the cold draft and confirms the fix with repeated readings. They document the method so the next class can learn from it.','يحدد الفريق تيار الهواء البارد ويتأكد من الحل بقياسات متكررة. ويوثق الطريقة ليستفيد منها الصف التالي.']},{text:'Replace the sensor immediately without checking it.',text_ar:'استبدل المستشعر فورًا دون فحصه.',response:'A new device may have the same problem if the cause is the environment around it.',response_ar:'قد يواجه الجهاز الجديد المشكلة نفسها إذا كان السبب في البيئة المحيطة به.',branchPage:['📦','The teacher pauses the order and asks the class to check the room conditions first.','يوقف المعلم طلب الشراء مؤقتًا ويطلب من الصف فحص ظروف الغرفة أولًا.'],endingPage:['🔬','The class finds the window gap, repairs it, and keeps the original sensor. They save the budget for a different experiment.','يجد الصف فجوة النافذة ويصلحها ويحتفظ بالمستشعر الأصلي. ويوفر الميزانية لتجربة أخرى.']},{text:'Choose the readings that support your first guess.',text_ar:'اختر القراءات التي تؤيد تخمينك الأول.',response:'Ignoring results that disagree with your idea can hide the real cause. Record every reading honestly.',response_ar:'قد يؤدي تجاهل النتائج المخالفة لفكرتك إلى إخفاء السبب الحقيقي. سجل كل قراءة بأمانة.',branchPage:['📊','Amina includes every measurement in the table and asks a classmate to check the pattern independently.','تدرج أمينة كل القياسات في الجدول وتطلب من زميل مراجعة النمط بصورة مستقلة.'],endingPage:['✅','The independent check confirms the conclusion and gives the class confidence in its evidence. Amina learns that honest data matters more than being right immediately.','يؤكد الفحص المستقل الاستنتاج ويمنح الصف الثقة في الأدلة. وتتعلم أمينة أن البيانات الصادقة أهم من إثبات صحة الرأي بسرعة.']}]},pages:[['🔬','The school science lab had been quiet for weeks because its old sensor kept giving strange readings. Everyone assumed the equipment was broken. The students had stopped volunteering for experiments because the results seemed random. Some believed the sensor was too old, while others thought the instructions were unclear. Their teacher was considering ordering a replacement, but Amina asked for one more afternoon to investigate before spending the budget.','ظل مختبر العلوم هادئًا لأسابيع لأن المستشعر القديم أعطى قراءات غريبة. افترض الجميع أن المعدات معطلة. توقف الطلاب عن التطوع للتجارب لأن النتائج بدت عشوائية. اعتقد بعضهم أن المستشعر قديم جدًا، بينما رأى آخرون أن التعليمات غير واضحة. كان المعلم يفكر في طلب جهاز بديل، لكن أمينة طلبت فترة بعد الظهر للتحقق قبل إنفاق الميزانية.'],['📒','When Amina checked the notes, she noticed that the readings changed whenever the window was open. She suggested testing the sensor in a closed room. Amina read the logbook from the previous month and compared the numbers with the weather notes. She found that the largest changes happened on cold mornings. Rather than guessing, she wrote a simple test plan: keep the sensor in one place, close the window, and record the readings every five minutes.','لاحظت أمينة أن القراءات تتغير كلما كانت النافذة مفتوحة، فاقترحت اختبار المستشعر في غرفة مغلقة. قرأت أمينة سجل المختبر للشهر السابق وقارنت الأرقام بملاحظات الطقس. وجدت أن أكبر التغيرات تحدث في الصباح البارد. وبدل التخمين، كتبت خطة اختبار بسيطة: إبقاء المستشعر في مكان واحد، وإغلاق النافذة، وتسجيل القراءات كل خمس دقائق.'],['🌡️','The next test confirmed her idea: a cold draft was affecting the instrument. After they sealed the window, the measurements became stable. The first set of readings still changed, so Amina checked the window frame and found a narrow gap. Cold air was reaching the sensor and changing its temperature. The team sealed the gap with removable tape, repeated the test, and watched the measurements settle into a steady pattern.','أكد الاختبار فكرتها: تيار هواء بارد كان يؤثر في الجهاز. بعد إغلاق النافذة، استقرت القياسات. استمرت القراءات الأولى في التغير، فتفقدت أمينة إطار النافذة ووجدت فجوة ضيقة. كان الهواء البارد يصل إلى المستشعر ويغير حرارته. أغلق الفريق الفجوة بشريط قابل للإزالة، وكرر الاختبار، وشاهد القراءات تستقر في نمط ثابت.'],['💡','The teacher praised Amina for looking for evidence instead of replacing the sensor. The lab soon became the busiest room in school. The teacher asked Amina to explain her method to the class. She showed the notes, the repeated measurements, and the evidence that supported the conclusion. The students returned to the lab with new questions. They had learned that careful testing can be more useful than quickly replacing equipment. For the Riverside Club open day, Mia, Sam, Nora, Leo, and Daniel help arrange the room. The sensor display becomes a favourite stop, and the friends agree to plan another event together.','أثنى المعلم على أمينة لأنها بحثت عن دليل بدل استبدال المستشعر. أصبح المختبر أكثر غرف المدرسة نشاطًا. طلب المعلم من أمينة شرح طريقتها للصف. عرضت الملاحظات والقياسات المتكررة والأدلة التي تدعم الاستنتاج. عاد الطلاب إلى المختبر ومعهم أسئلة جديدة. لقد تعلموا أن الاختبار الدقيق قد يكون أنفع من استبدال المعدات بسرعة. في اليوم المفتوح لنادي ريفرسايد، تساعد ميا وسام ونورا وليو ودانيال في ترتيب القاعة. ويصبح عرض المستشعر محطة محببة للزوار، ويتفق الأصدقاء على التخطيط لفعالية أخرى معًا.']],vocab:{sensor:['a device that detects or measures something','مستشعر','SEN-sər','The sensor measures the temperature.'],assumed:['believed something without checking','افترض','uh-SOOMD','I assumed the shop was open.'],draft:['a current of air in a room','تيار هواء','draft','A cold draft came through the window.'],evidence:['facts that help show what is true','دليل','EV-i-dens','We need evidence before deciding.']},questions:[['What caused the strange readings?',['A cold draft from the window','A broken computer','A missing notebook'],0,'The sensor was affected by cold air entering through the open window.'],['What does “assumed” mean?',['Believed without checking','Measured carefully','Explained to a group'],0,'Everyone thought the equipment was broken before testing the idea.'],['Why did the teacher praise Amina?',['She looked for evidence','She bought equipment','She finished first'],0,'Amina investigated the cause instead of replacing the sensor immediately.']]},
{id:'b2-open-door',title:'The Open Door',level:'B2',tone:'#C49BE8',emoji:'🚪',minutes:6,decision:{afterPage:1,prompt:'A colleague seems reluctant to join a new project. What is the best response?',prompt_ar:'يبدو أن زميلًا متردد في الانضمام إلى مشروع جديد. ما أفضل تصرف؟',options:[{text:'Ask what concerns them and listen before proposing a solution.',text_ar:'اسأل عمّا يقلقه واستمع قبل اقتراح حل.',response:'This invites an honest explanation and helps you respond to the real concern instead of making assumptions.',response_ar:'هذا يتيح حوارًا صريحًا ويساعدك على معالجة سبب القلق الحقيقي بدلًا من الافتراض.',branchPage:['☕','In a private conversation, your colleague explains that the project deadline clashes with another commitment.','في حديث خاص، يشرح زميلك أن موعد المشروع يتعارض مع التزام آخر.'],endingPage:['☕','You agree on a realistic task split. Your colleague joins the project, and the team starts with clearer expectations.','تتفقان على تقسيم واقعي للمهام. ينضم زميلك إلى المشروع ويبدأ الفريق بتوقعات أوضح.']},{text:'Tell the whole team that they are being difficult.',text_ar:'أخبر الفريق كله بأنه يتصرف بصعوبة.',response:'Public blame can damage trust and does not explain the hesitation. A private, respectful conversation is more useful.',response_ar:'قد يضر اللوم العلني بالثقة ولا يوضح سبب التردد. الحوار الخاص والمحترم أنفع.',branchPage:['🤝','After the meeting, you ask your colleague privately what made the project difficult to accept.','بعد الاجتماع، تسأل زميلك على انفراد عمّا جعله مترددًا في قبول المشروع.'],endingPage:['🤝','You discover a workload conflict and adjust responsibilities together. The relationship stays professional and the project moves forward.','تكتشف تعارضًا في عبء العمل وتعدّلان المسؤوليات معًا. تبقى العلاقة مهنية ويتقدم المشروع.']},{text:'Promise that there are no risks, even though you are unsure.',text_ar:'عده بعدم وجود مخاطر رغم عدم تأكدك.',response:'An unsupported promise may create more problems later. Be transparent about what is known and what still needs checking.',response_ar:'قد يسبب الوعد غير المدعوم مشكلات لاحقًا. كن واضحًا بشأن ما تعرفه وما يحتاج إلى تحقق.',branchPage:['📋','You explain what is known, list the remaining risks, and suggest checking them before making promises.','توضح ما تعرفه، وتدوّن المخاطر المتبقية، وتقترح التحقق منها قبل تقديم الوعود.'],endingPage:['📋','The team creates a short risk plan. Your honesty builds trust and gives everyone a clearer way to proceed.','يضع الفريق خطة قصيرة للمخاطر. تبني صراحتك الثقة وتمنح الجميع طريقة أوضح للتقدم.']}]},pages:[['🏢','The new manager inherited a team that rarely spoke up. Meetings were polished but unproductive, and promising ideas were routinely swept under the rug. The manager, Elena, had joined the company after a period of rapid growth. The team looked efficient from the outside, yet projects moved slowly and people often waited for permission. She initially assumed that the staff needed clearer targets, but she wanted to understand the reasons before changing the rules.','ورث المدير فريقًا نادرًا ما يتحدث بصراحة. كانت الاجتماعات مرتبة لكنها غير منتجة، وكانت الأفكار الواعدة تُخفى باستمرار. انضمت المديرة إلينا إلى الشركة بعد فترة من النمو السريع. بدا الفريق فعالًا من الخارج، لكن المشاريع كانت تتقدم ببطء وكان الموظفون ينتظرون الإذن كثيرًا. افترضت في البداية أنهم يحتاجون إلى أهداف أوضح، لكنها أرادت فهم الأسباب قبل تغيير القواعد.'],['🗣️','Rather than imposing more rules, she invited everyone to share one concern anonymously. At first, the feedback was blunt; nevertheless, she listened without becoming defensive. She invited the team to send concerns without names and promised to discuss the patterns rather than search for a person to blame. Some messages were uncomfortable to read. Elena resisted the urge to defend every past decision and instead asked which daily steps were creating unnecessary delays.','بدل فرض قواعد أخرى، دعت الجميع إلى مشاركة مشكلة دون أسماء. كان النقد صريحًا، ومع ذلك استمعت دون دفاعية. دعت الفريق إلى إرسال الملاحظات دون أسماء، ووعدت بمناقشة الأنماط بدل البحث عن شخص تلقي عليه اللوم. كانت بعض الرسائل غير مريحة. قاومت إلينا رغبتها في الدفاع عن كل قرار سابق، وسألت بدلًا من ذلك عن الخطوات اليومية التي تسبب تأخيرًا غير ضروري.'],['🧩','Several comments pointed to the same bottleneck: every small decision required her approval. She had tried to keep things on track, but the process was holding the team back. One message explained that even small purchases and routine schedule changes waited in her inbox. Elena had believed that reviewing everything would prevent mistakes, but the process had made the team dependent on her. She met with two colleagues and designed clear limits for decisions they could make themselves.','أشارت التعليقات إلى العائق نفسه: كل قرار صغير يحتاج موافقتها. كانت تحاول إبقاء الأمور منظمة لكن العملية أعاقت الفريق. أوضحت إحدى الرسائل أن المشتريات الصغيرة والتغييرات الروتينية في الجدول تنتظر في صندوق رسائلها. كانت إلينا تعتقد أن مراجعة كل شيء ستمنع الأخطاء، لكن العملية جعلت الفريق يعتمد عليها. اجتمعت بزميلين ووضعت حدودًا واضحة للقرارات التي يمكنهم اتخاذها بأنفسهم.'],['🌱','She delegated routine choices and kept the door open for difficult conversations. Within a month, the team took ownership and its hidden ideas began to flourish. The change did not solve every problem immediately. A few decisions had to be corrected, and the team reviewed what had gone wrong without hiding it. After several weeks, meetings became shorter and people shared ideas earlier. Elena learned that trust grows when responsibility is clear and feedback is safe.','فوّضت القرارات الروتينية وأبقت الباب مفتوحًا للمحادثات الصعبة. خلال شهر، تحمل الفريق المسؤولية وبدأت أفكاره المخفية تزدهر. لم يحل التغيير كل المشكلات فورًا. احتاجت بعض القرارات إلى التصحيح، وراجع الفريق الأخطاء دون إخفائها. وبعد أسابيع، أصبحت الاجتماعات أقصر وبدأ الناس بمشاركة أفكارهم مبكرًا. تعلمت إلينا أن الثقة تنمو عندما تكون المسؤولية واضحة وتكون الملاحظات آمنة.']],vocab:{'speak up':['to express an opinion openly','يتحدث بصراحة','speek up','Please speak up if you disagree.'],'swept':['hidden instead of being dealt with','أُخفي بدل معالجة المشكلة','swept','The mistake was swept under the rug.'],bottleneck:['a point that slows progress','عائق يبطئ التقدم','BOT-ul-nek','Approval became a bottleneck.'],delegated:['gave a task or decision to another person','فوّض','DEL-uh-gay-tid','She delegated some tasks.'],ownership:['acceptance of responsibility','تحمّل المسؤولية','OH-ner-ship','The team took ownership of the project.']},questions:[['Why were the meetings unproductive?',['People hid concerns and ideas','They were too short','The manager cancelled them'],0,'People rarely spoke up, so useful ideas stayed hidden.'],['What does “swept under the rug” mean?',['Hidden rather than addressed','Cleaned carefully','Shared with everyone'],0,'Problems were not openly discussed.'],['What changed after delegation?',['The team took more responsibility','All meetings stopped','The team became smaller'],0,'Giving people authority helped them take ownership.']]},
{id:'b2-second-chance',title:'A Second Chance',level:'B2',tone:'#E99BAF',emoji:'🎭',minutes:6,pages:[['🎤','Rafi had spent months preparing for a public speaking contest, yet he froze halfway through his opening. He was convinced he had blown his only chance. Rafi had imagined the contest many times: the bright stage, the judges, and the applause at the end. He had prepared strong examples and memorised his opening. Yet when he saw the audience, his mouth went dry and the next sentence disappeared from his mind. He rushed, stopped, and left the stage disappointed.','استعد رافي أشهرًا لمسابقة الخطابة، لكنه تجمد في منتصف مقدمته. اقتنع أنه أضاع فرصته الوحيدة. تخيل رافي المسابقة مرات كثيرة: المنصة المضيئة والحكام والتصفيق في النهاية. حضر أمثلة قوية وحفظ مقدمته. لكنه عندما رأى الجمهور جف حلقه واختفت الجملة التالية من ذهنه. استعجل ثم توقف وغادر المنصة خائب الأمل.'],['📝','His coach refused to sugar-coat the result, but reminded him that one bad performance did not define his ability. They reviewed the recording together. His coach, Maya, watched the recording with him the following day. She did not pretend that the speech had gone well, but she separated the performance from his ability. They noticed that he looked down whenever he lost a word and tried to fill every silence. These were habits they could practise changing.','رفضت مدربته تجميل النتيجة، لكنها ذكّرته بأن أداءً سيئًا واحدًا لا يحدد قدرته. راجعا التسجيل معًا. شاهدت مدربته مايا التسجيل معه في اليوم التالي. لم تتظاهر بأن الخطاب كان جيدًا، لكنها فصلت بين الأداء وقدرته. لاحظا أنه ينظر إلى الأسفل كلما نسي كلمة ويحاول ملء كل لحظة صمت. كانت هذه عادات يمكنهما التدرب على تغييرها.'],['🪞','Over the next few weeks, Rafi practised in front of friends and learned to pause when he lost his place. Gradually, he stopped treating every mistake as a disaster. For several weeks, Rafi practised in small steps. First he spoke to two friends, then to a club, and finally to a larger group. Maya taught him to pause, breathe, and return to his main point when he lost his place. The pauses felt uncomfortable at first, but soon sounded natural.','خلال الأسابيع التالية، تدرب رافي أمام أصدقائه وتعلم التوقف حين يفقد تسلسل كلامه. تدريجيًا توقف عن اعتبار كل خطأ كارثة. تدرب رافي لأسابيع بخطوات صغيرة. تحدث أولًا أمام صديقين، ثم أمام نادٍ، وأخيرًا أمام مجموعة أكبر. علمته مايا التوقف والتنفس والعودة إلى فكرته الرئيسية إذا فقد تسلسل كلامه. بدت فترات الصمت محرجة في البداية، لكنها أصبحت طبيعية لاحقًا.'],['🏆','At the next event, he delivered a calmer speech. He did not win, but listeners approached him afterward, and he turned a setback into useful experience. At the next event, Rafi delivered a calmer speech and made one small mistake without losing his focus. He did not win the prize, but several listeners asked him about his ideas afterward. On the way home, he felt proud for a different reason: he had learned how to continue after a difficult moment.','في الفعالية التالية، ألقى خطابًا أهدأ. لم يفز، لكن مستمعين اقتربوا منه، وحوّل العثرة إلى خبرة مفيدة. في الفعالية التالية، ألقى رافي خطابًا أهدأ وارتكب خطأ صغيرًا دون أن يفقد تركيزه. لم يفز بالجائزة، لكن عدة مستمعين سألوه عن أفكاره بعد ذلك. وفي طريق العودة، شعر بالفخر لسبب مختلف: لقد تعلم كيف يواصل بعد لحظة صعبة.']],vocab:{froze:['became unable to move or speak from fear','تجمّد من الخوف','frohz','I froze when everyone looked at me.'],'blown':['lost an opportunity through a mistake','أضاع فرصة','blohn','He thought he had blown his chance.'],'sugar-coat':['make something unpleasant sound better than it is','يجمّل الحقيقة','SHUG-er koht','I will not sugar-coat the feedback.'],setback:['a problem that delays progress','عثرة أو انتكاسة','SET-bak','A setback can teach you something.']},questions:[['Why did Rafi think he had failed?',['He froze during his speech','He forgot to attend','He lost his notes'],0,'He became unable to continue smoothly during the opening.'],['What does “sugar-coat” mean?',['Make bad news sound less bad','Prepare a dessert','Repeat a speech'],0,'The coach was honest instead of making the result sound better.'],['What did Rafi learn?',['Mistakes can become useful experience','He should never speak again','Winning is the only goal'],0,'He improved and gained confidence even without winning.']]}
,{id:'c1-quiet-objection',title:'The Quiet Objection',level:'C1',tone:'#A9B7E8',emoji:'🗣️',minutes:6,pages:[['🏢','Leila reviews a project schedule that assumes every supplier will deliver on time. The launch date looks realistic only if that assumption holds.','تراجع ليلى جدول مشروع يفترض أن جميع الموردين سيسلّمون في الموعد. يبدو موعد الإطلاق واقعيًا فقط إذا صحّ هذا الافتراض.'],['📝','Instead of rejecting the plan outright, she asks which delivery estimates are supported by evidence and which are still uncertain. The room falls quiet.','بدل رفض الخطة مباشرة، تسأل عن مواعيد التسليم المدعومة بالأدلة وتلك التي ما زالت غير مؤكدة. يعمّ الصمت الغرفة.'],['🔍','The team checks recent supplier records and discovers that one critical component often arrives late. Leila suggests comparing the cost of a small delay with the cost of keeping a backup supplier.','يراجع الفريق سجلات الموردين الحديثة ويكتشف أن أحد المكوّنات الأساسية يتأخر كثيرًا. تقترح ليلى مقارنة تكلفة التأخير القصير بتكلفة تجهيز مورد بديل.'],['🤝','The team adds a contingency and adjusts the schedule before the problem occurs. Leila’s measured objection protects the launch date—and shows that challenging an assumption can strengthen a plan.','يضيف الفريق خطة احتياطية ويعدّل الجدول قبل وقوع المشكلة. يحمي اعتراض ليلى المتزن موعد الإطلاق، ويُظهر أن مراجعة الافتراضات قد تجعل الخطة أقوى.']],decision:{afterPage:1,prompt:'The team is uncomfortable with Leila’s question. What should she do next?',prompt_ar:'يشعر الفريق بعدم الارتياح تجاه سؤال ليلى. ماذا ينبغي أن تفعل بعد ذلك؟',options:[{text:'Ask for the evidence behind the estimates and invite the team to review it together.',text_ar:'اطلب الأدلة التي تستند إليها التقديرات وادعُ الفريق إلى مراجعتها معًا.',response:'This keeps the discussion focused on evidence, gives colleagues a shared problem to solve, and avoids turning the question into a personal confrontation.',response_ar:'يبقي ذلك النقاش قائمًا على الأدلة، ويمنح الزملاء مشكلة مشتركة لحلها، ويمنع تحول السؤال إلى مواجهة شخصية.',branchPage:['📊','Leila asks the team to compare the supplier estimates with recent delivery records before deciding.','تطلب ليلى من الفريق مقارنة تقديرات الموردين بسجلات التسليم الحديثة قبل اتخاذ القرار.'],endingPage:['📊','The records reveal a risk early. The team adds a backup supplier and keeps the launch plan credible.','تكشف السجلات الخطر مبكرًا. يضيف الفريق موردًا بديلًا ويحافظ على واقعية خطة الإطلاق.']},{text:'Withdraw the concern so the meeting can finish on time.',text_ar:'تراجع عن مخاوفك كي ينتهي الاجتماع في موعده.',response:'This may preserve short-term comfort, but the uncertainty remains hidden and the team loses a chance to reduce the risk.',response_ar:'قد يحافظ ذلك على الراحة مؤقتًا، لكن الغموض سيظل مخفيًا وستضيع فرصة تقليل المخاطر.',branchPage:['🤐','Leila lets the meeting end, but later notices that no one has checked the delivery assumptions.','تترك ليلى الاجتماع ينتهي، لكنها تلاحظ لاحقًا أن أحدًا لم يتحقق من افتراضات التسليم.'],endingPage:['🤐','A follow-up review uncovers the delay risk later than it should have. Leila raises it again, and the team builds a contingency under more pressure.','تكشف مراجعة لاحقة خطر التأخير بعد فوات وقت مناسب. تطرحه ليلى مجددًا ويضع الفريق خطة احتياطية تحت ضغط أكبر.']},{text:'Insist that the schedule is wrong before checking the records.',text_ar:'أصرّ على أن الجدول خاطئ قبل مراجعة السجلات.',response:'Raising a risk matters, but declaring the plan wrong before checking evidence can weaken trust and make a useful concern easier to dismiss.',response_ar:'من المهم طرح المخاطر، لكن إعلان خطأ الخطة قبل التحقق من الأدلة قد يضعف الثقة ويجعل تجاهل الملاحظة أسهل.',branchPage:['🔍','Leila realises her claim is too strong and proposes checking the records before judging the schedule.','تدرك ليلى أن حكمها كان قاطعًا أكثر من اللازم، وتقترح مراجعة السجلات قبل تقييم الجدول.'],endingPage:['🔍','The evidence gives the team a specific problem to solve. Leila earns trust by revising her claim and helping build a stronger plan.','تمنح الأدلة الفريق مشكلة محددة لحلها. وتكسب ليلى الثقة حين تراجع حكمها وتساعد على بناء خطة أقوى.']}]},vocab:{assumption:['something accepted as true without complete proof','افتراض','uh-SUMP-shun','The plan rests on an assumption.'],contingency:['a plan for a possible problem','خطة احتياطية','kun-TIN-juhn-see','We prepared a contingency.'],measured:['calm and carefully considered','متزن ومدروس','MEZH-erd','She gave a measured response.'],outright:['completely or immediately, without hesitation','بشكل قاطع','OWT-ryte','He did not reject the idea outright.'],estimate:['a careful guess about an amount, cost, or time','تقدير','ES-ti-mit','The delivery estimate was too optimistic.'],critical:['extremely important to success','أساسي / بالغ الأهمية','KRIT-i-kəl','The critical component arrived late.'],withdraw:['to take back or remove something','يتراجع عن / يسحب','with-DRAW','She decided not to withdraw her concern.']},questions:[['Why does Leila question the schedule?',['It relies on untested assumptions','She dislikes the supplier','She wants to cancel the project'],0,'The schedule depends on every supplier delivering on time, but this has not been verified.'],['What is a contingency in this context?',['A backup plan for a possible problem','A final invoice','A meeting summary'],0,'A contingency prepares the team for a risk, such as a late delivery.'],['What is the strongest lesson from the story?',['Evidence-based objections can improve a plan','Disagreement always harms teams','A plan should never change'],0,'Leila checks the evidence, raises the risk constructively, and helps the team prepare before the problem occurs.']]}
,{id:'c1-cost-of-clarity',title:'The Cost of Clarity',level:'C1',tone:'#8BCFC2',emoji:'🔎',minutes:5,pages:[["📊","A consultancy circulates a report claiming that the new scheduling process is faster. Omar notices that the figures omit the extra hours spent on maintenance.","تُوزّع شركة استشارية تقريرًا يزعم أن عملية الجدولة الجديدة أسرع. يلاحظ عمر أن الأرقام تُغفل ساعات الصيانة الإضافية."],["🧾","He asks the authors to disclose the hidden costs. At first they hesitate, because every caveat seems to weaken the headline result.","يطلب من المؤلفين الكشف عن التكاليف الخفية. يترددون في البداية لأن كل تحفّظ يبدو كأنه يُضعف النتيجة الرئيسية."],["⚖️","Omar replies that every improvement involves a compromise, and readers deserve to see it. Leaving the cost out would not remove it; it would only move it onto someone else.","يردّ عمر بأن كل تحسين يتضمن مقايضة، وأن القرّاء يستحقون رؤيتها. حذف التكلفة لا يزيلها، بل ينقلها إلى شخص آخر."],["💡","The authors agree to qualify their claim: the process is faster, but only if maintenance is planned in advance. The revised report sounds less dramatic, yet it is far more useful to decision-makers.","يوافق المؤلفون على تقييد ادعائهم: العملية أسرع، لكن فقط إذا خُطّطت الصيانة مسبقًا. يبدو التقرير المعدّل أقل إثارة، لكنه أنفع بكثير لصنّاع القرار."]],vocab:{omit:["to leave something out","يغفل","oh-MIT","The summary omitted a key cost."],disclose:["to make something known that was hidden","يكشف","dis-KLOHZ","The company disclosed the risks."],compromise:["a balance in which each side gives something up","حل وسط","KOM-pruh-myz","Speed often means a compromise on quality."],qualify:["to limit a claim by stating the conditions","يقيّد","KWOL-ih-fy","She qualified her claim with a warning."]},questions:[["What does Omar notice about the report?",["The figures leave out maintenance hours","The title is misleading","The authors are unknown"],0,"The report omits the extra maintenance time."],["Why do the authors hesitate?",["Caveats seem to weaken their headline result","They have lost the data","They disagree about the date"],0,"Every limitation seems to make the result less impressive."],["What does Omar mean by moving the cost onto someone else?",["Hiding a cost does not remove it","The authors will pay for it","The readers will ignore it"],0,"The cost still exists; someone else will have to bear it."],["What does it mean to qualify a claim?",["To state the conditions under which it is true","To repeat it more loudly","To delete the evidence"],0,"A qualified claim says when and how far it applies."]]}
,{id:'c2-language-of-consensus',title:'The Language of Consensus',level:'C2',tone:'#C6A7E8',emoji:'⚖️',minutes:6,decision:{afterPage:1,prompt:'A meeting reaches quick agreement, but one important risk has not been examined. What should you do?',prompt_ar:'توصل الاجتماع إلى اتفاق سريع، لكن خطرًا مهمًا لم يُفحص. ماذا ينبغي أن تفعل؟',options:[{text:'Name the unresolved risk neutrally and ask the group to test the assumption.',text_ar:'اذكر الخطر الذي لم يُحسم بحياد واطلب من المجموعة اختبار الافتراض.',response:'This protects the quality of the decision without turning disagreement into a personal conflict. Consensus is stronger when important uncertainty has been examined.',response_ar:'يحافظ ذلك على جودة القرار دون تحويل الاختلاف إلى خلاف شخصي. يكون الاتفاق أقوى عندما تُفحص أوجه عدم اليقين المهمة.',branchPage:['📊','You ask the group to test the assumption against the available evidence before recording the decision.','تطلب من المجموعة اختبار الافتراض بالأدلة المتاحة قبل تسجيل القرار.'],endingPage:['📊','The evidence reveals a hidden cost. The group adjusts the proposal and records why, reaching a more defensible agreement.','تكشف الأدلة تكلفة خفية. يعدّل الفريق المقترح ويسجل الأسباب، فيصل إلى اتفاق أقوى.']},{text:'Stay silent because everyone else agrees.',text_ar:'التزم الصمت لأن الجميع موافقون.',response:'Silence can preserve the mood, but it leaves the risk unexamined. A concise, evidence-focused question can improve the decision.',response_ar:'قد يحافظ الصمت على الأجواء الهادئة، لكنه يترك الخطر دون فحص. يمكن لسؤال موجز يستند إلى الأدلة تحسين القرار.',branchPage:['🗣️','You raise the concern after the meeting and ask the chair to reopen the risk for a brief review.','تثير مخاوفك بعد الاجتماع وتطلب مراجعة قصيرة للمخاطر.'],endingPage:['🗣️','The team schedules a focused review. The delay is small, but it prevents a costly misunderstanding later.','يحدد الفريق موعدًا لمراجعة مركزة. التأخير بسيط لكنه يمنع سوء فهم مكلفًا لاحقًا.']},{text:'Reject the whole proposal without explaining why.',text_ar:'ارفض المقترح كله دون توضيح السبب.',response:'A firm rejection without evidence may stop useful discussion. Identify the specific risk and invite the group to evaluate it.',response_ar:'قد يؤدي الرفض دون دليل إلى إيقاف نقاش مفيد. حدّد الخطر بعينه وادعُ المجموعة إلى تقييمه.',branchPage:['⚖️','You explain the specific risk and propose a quick test instead of rejecting the entire proposal.','تشرح الخطر المحدد وتقترح اختبارًا سريعًا بدلًا من رفض المقترح كله.'],endingPage:['⚖️','The test shows which part of the proposal needs changing. The group keeps the useful ideas and revises the risky assumption.','يكشف الاختبار الجزء الذي يحتاج إلى تعديل. يحتفظ الفريق بالأفكار المفيدة ويصحح الافتراض الخطر.']}]},pages:[["🏛️","A planning committee approves a proposal unanimously. Mariam, who chairs the meeting, is not reassured: several members have said nothing at all.","توافق لجنة التخطيط على مقترح بالإجماع. لكن مريم، التي ترأس الاجتماع، لا تطمئن؛ فهناك أعضاء لم ينطقوا بكلمة."],["🧩","She distinguishes genuine agreement from mere acquiescence. Silence, she says, may reflect fatigue, deference or fear of appearing disloyal rather than conviction.","تميّز بين الاتفاق الحقيقي والإذعان المجرد. تقول إن الصمت قد يعكس التعب أو الإجلال أو الخوف من الظهور بمظهر غير الوفيّ، لا القناعة."],["🗣️","Before the vote is recorded, Mariam invites dissent in specific terms: what would have to be true for this plan to fail? Two members then raise concerns that nobody had anticipated.","قبل تسجيل التصويت، تدعو مريم إلى إبداء الرأي المخالف بعبارات محددة: ما الذي يجب أن يحدث كي تفشل هذه الخطة؟ عندها يثير عضوان مخاوف لم يتوقعها أحد."],["🌱","The proposal is revised, and the final decision gains broader support precisely because opposing views were examined rather than avoided.","يُعدَّل المقترح، ويحظى القرار النهائي بدعم أوسع تحديدًا لأن الآراء المعارضة فُحصت ولم تُتجنَّب."]],vocab:{unanimously:["with everyone in agreement","بالإجماع","yoo-NAN-uh-mus-lee","The board voted unanimously."],acquiescence:["acceptance without protest","إذعان","ak-wee-ES-ens","Silence is not always acquiescence."],deference:["respectful yielding to another person's opinion","إجلال وانصياع","DEF-er-ens","He spoke with deference to the senior staff."],dissent:["a different opinion expressed openly","رأي مخالف","dih-SENT","The chair welcomed dissent."]},questions:[["Why is Mariam not reassured by the vote?",["Several members stayed silent","The vote was close","The proposal was too long"],0,"Unanimous approval may hide unspoken doubts."],["What may silence reflect, according to Mariam?",["Fatigue, deference or fear","Total agreement","Lack of interest in the topic"],0,"Silence is not reliable evidence of conviction."],["How does she invite dissent?",["By asking what would make the plan fail","By repeating the proposal","By ending the meeting"],0,"A specific question makes it easier to voice doubts."],["Why does the final decision gain support?",["Opposing views were examined","Disagreement was banned","The vote was faster"],0,"Examining dissent strengthens the outcome."]]}
,{id:'c2-unintended-inference',title:'The Unintended Inference',level:'C2',tone:'#E9A9B6',emoji:'🧠',minutes:6,pages:[["📩","In a review meeting, a director describes a colleague's proposal as “ambitious.” Some listeners hear praise; others infer that she considers it unrealistic.","في اجتماع مراجعة، تصف مديرة مقترح زميل بأنه «طموح». يسمع بعض الحاضرين مديحًا، بينما يستنتج آخرون أنها تراه غير واقعي."],["💬","Nabil, the author, is uncertain which meaning was intended. He asks what evidence would distinguish genuine encouragement from polite scepticism.","نبيل، صاحب المقترح، غير متأكد من المعنى المقصود. يسأل عن الأدلة التي تميّز التشجيع الحقيقي من التشكيك المهذب."],["🧭","The director concedes that the word was ambiguous. She explains that the goal is worthwhile, but several milestones need clearer justification.","تعترف المديرة بأن الكلمة كانت غامضة. توضح أن الهدف جدير بالاهتمام، لكن عدة مراحل رئيسية تحتاج إلى تبرير أوضح."],["✅","Nabil revises the plan accordingly. The episode shows how an implication can travel further than the words themselves, and why it is wise to ask rather than assume.","يعدّل نبيل الخطة وفق ذلك. تُظهر الواقعة كيف يمكن أن يصل المعنى الضمني أبعد من الكلمات نفسها، ولماذا من الحكمة أن نسأل بدل أن نفترض."]],vocab:{infer:["to reach a conclusion from clues rather than from direct statement","يستنتج","in-FUR","Listeners may infer criticism."],ambiguous:["having more than one possible meaning","غامض","am-BIG-yoo-us","The instructions were ambiguous."],milestones:["important stages in a process","مراحل رئيسية","MYL-stohnz","Each milestone needs an owner."]},questions:[["Why is “ambitious” interpreted differently?",["Its implication depends on context and tone","No adjective was used","The proposal was hidden"],0,"The word can signal praise or doubt."],["What does Nabil ask for?",["Evidence that distinguishes encouragement from scepticism","A new director","A shorter report"],0,"He wants a way to tell the two meanings apart."],["What does the director admit?",["The word was ambiguous","The goal is worthless","The meeting was unnecessary"],0,"She concedes her wording was unclear."],["What lesson does the story suggest?",["Ask for clarification instead of assuming","Never use positive words","Avoid review meetings"],0,"An implication can travel further than the words themselves."]]},
{"id":"a1-blue-umbrella","title":"The Blue Umbrella","level":"A1","tone":"#82BDE8","emoji":"☂️","minutes":3,"pages":[["🌦️","It is raining. Ana has a blue umbrella.","إنها تمطر. لدى آنا مظلة زرقاء."],["🚌","At the bus stop, she sees an old man without an umbrella.","في موقف الحافلة، ترى رجلًا مسنًا بلا مظلة."],["🙂","Ana shares her umbrella with him. They get on the bus together.","تشاركه آنا مظلتها. يصعدان إلى الحافلة معًا."]],"vocab":{"umbrella":["a cover that keeps rain off you","مظلة","um-BREL-uh","Take an umbrella when it rains."],"share":["to use or give something together","يشارك","shair","I share my book with my friend."],"rain":["water that falls from clouds","مطر","rayn","The rain is cold."],"together":["with another person or group","معًا","tuh-GETH-er","We walk together."]},"questions":[["What is the weather like?",["Rainy","Very hot","Snowy"],0,"The first page says it is raining."],["Who has no umbrella?",["An old man","Ana's teacher","The bus driver"],0,"Ana sees an old man without an umbrella."],["What does Ana do?",["She shares her umbrella","She goes home","She buys a bus"],0,"Ana helps the man by sharing her umbrella."]]},
{"id":"a1-helpful-neighbor","title":"A Helpful Neighbor","level":"A1","tone":"#8CC7A1","emoji":"🪴","minutes":3,"pages":[["🏡","Ben has a small garden. He waters the flowers every morning.","لدى بن حديقة صغيرة. يسقي الأزهار كل صباح."],["🪣","One day, his water bucket breaks. The flowers are dry.","في أحد الأيام، ينكسر دلو الماء. تصبح الأزهار جافة."],["🌷","His neighbor gives him a new bucket. Ben waters the flowers and says thank you.","تعطيه جارته دلوًا جديدًا. يسقي بن الأزهار ويشكرها."]],"vocab":{"neighbor":["a person who lives near you","جار","NAY-ber","My neighbor lives next door."],"bucket":["a container for carrying water","دلو","BUK-it","The bucket is full of water."],"water":["the clear liquid people drink and use for plants","ماء","WAW-ter","Plants need water."],"broken":["damaged and not working","مكسور","BROH-ken","The old cup is broken."]},"questions":[["What does Ben do every morning?",["Waters the flowers","Paints the house","Cooks soup"],0,"Ben waters his garden each morning."],["Why are the flowers dry?",["His bucket breaks","It is winter","He sells them"],0,"The broken bucket makes watering difficult."],["How does the neighbor help?",["She gives him a bucket","She cuts the flowers","She takes his garden"],0,"She gives Ben a new bucket."]]},
{"id":"a1-wrong-lunchbox","title":"The Wrong Lunchbox","level":"A1","tone":"#E8B77E","emoji":"🍱","minutes":3,"pages":[["🏫","Lina takes a yellow lunchbox to school. It has a sandwich and an apple.","تأخذ لينا علبة طعام صفراء إلى المدرسة. فيها شطيرة وتفاحة."],["🍎","At lunch, she opens it and finds a note. The food is not hers.","وقت الغداء، تفتحها وتجد ورقة. الطعام ليس لها."],["🤝","Lina checks the name. She gives the lunchbox to Omar and finds her own.","تتحقق لينا من الاسم. تعطي علبة الطعام لعمر وتجد علبتها."]],"vocab":{"lunchbox":["a box used to carry food","علبة طعام","LUNCH-boks","My lunchbox is in my bag."],"sandwich":["food made with filling between bread","شطيرة","SAND-wich","I eat a cheese sandwich."],"note":["a short piece of writing","ملاحظة","noht","There is a note on the table."],"own":["belonging to you","خاص بك","ohn","This is my own bag."]},"questions":[["What color is Lina's lunchbox?",["Yellow","Blue","Green"],0,"Lina takes a yellow lunchbox to school."],["What does Lina find inside?",["A note","A toy car","A key"],0,"She opens the box and finds a note."],["How does Lina solve the problem?",["She checks the name","She throws the food away","She hides the box"],0,"She checks the name and returns Omar's lunchbox."]]},
{"id":"a1-note-grandma","title":"A Note for Grandma","level":"A1","tone":"#E8A9C3","emoji":"💌","minutes":3,"pages":[["✏️","Tom wants to visit Grandma. He writes a short note for her.","يريد توم زيارة جدته. يكتب لها رسالة قصيرة."],["🚲","He puts the note in his bag and rides his bike to her house.","يضع الرسالة في حقيبته ويركب دراجته إلى منزلها."],["❤️","Grandma reads the note and smiles. They make tea and talk.","تقرأ الجدة الرسالة وتبتسم. يحضّران الشاي ويتحدثان."]],"vocab":{"visit":["to go and see a person or place","يزور","VIZ-it","We visit Grandma on Sunday."],"write":["to make words with a pen or keyboard","يكتب","ryt","I write a short note."],"smile":["to make a happy expression","يبتسم","smyl","She smiles at her friend."],"tea":["a hot drink made with leaves","شاي","tee","Grandma makes tea."]},"questions":[["Who does Tom want to visit?",["His grandma","His coach","His neighbor"],0,"Tom wants to visit Grandma."],["Where does he put the note?",["In his bag","Under a tree","On the bus"],0,"He puts the note in his bag."],["How does Grandma feel when she reads it?",["Happy","Angry","Sleepy"],0,"Grandma smiles after reading the note."]]},
{"id":"a2-library-card","title":"The Library Card","level":"A2","tone":"#8BB6E8","emoji":"📚","minutes":3,"pages":[["📖","Nora wants to borrow a mystery book, but she has never used the town library.","تريد نورا استعارة كتاب غموض، لكنها لم تستخدم مكتبة المدينة من قبل."],["🪪","The librarian explains that she needs a library card and a form with her address.","تشرح أمينة المكتبة أنها تحتاج إلى بطاقة مكتبة واستمارة تتضمن عنوانها."],["✨","Nora fills in the form, receives her card, and borrows the book for two weeks.","تملأ نورا الاستمارة وتحصل على بطاقتها وتستعير الكتاب لمدة أسبوعين."]],"vocab":{"borrow":["to take something for a time and return it later","يستعير","BOR-oh","You can borrow books from a library."],"librarian":["a person who works in a library","أمين مكتبة","ly-BRAIR-ee-un","The librarian helped me find a book."],"form":["a document you fill in with information","استمارة","form","Please complete this form."],"address":["the details of where someone lives","عنوان","uh-DRES","Write your address here."]},"questions":[["What does Nora want to borrow?",["A mystery book","A bicycle","A cooking pot"],0,"Nora wants to borrow a mystery book."],["What does she need before borrowing?",["A library card and a form","A train ticket","A school uniform"],0,"The librarian explains the card and form requirements."],["How long can Nora keep the book?",["Two weeks","One day","One year"],0,"The story says she borrows it for two weeks."]]},
{"id":"a2-room-for-two","title":"A Room for Two","level":"A2","tone":"#C3A7E8","emoji":"🛏️","minutes":3,"pages":[["🧳","Maya and her cousin arrive at a small hotel after a long journey. They booked one room.","تصل مايا وابن عمها إلى فندق صغير بعد رحلة طويلة. لقد حجزا غرفة واحدة."],["🔑","At reception, the clerk finds their booking but notices that the room has only one bed.","في الاستقبال، يجد الموظف الحجز لكنه يلاحظ أن الغرفة فيها سرير واحد فقط."],["🛎️","Maya explains their needs politely. The clerk checks another room and gives them a room with two beds.","تشرح مايا احتياجاتهما بأدب. يفحص الموظف غرفة أخرى ويمنحهما غرفة بسريرين."]],"vocab":{"booking":["an arrangement made in advance","حجز","BOOK-ing","Our booking is for Friday."],"reception":["the desk where guests arrive at a hotel","الاستقبال","ri-SEP-shun","Ask at reception for your key."],"clerk":["a person who works at a desk or counter","موظف","klurk","The clerk checked our booking."],"politely":["in a respectful way","بأدب","puh-LYTE-lee","She asked politely for help."]},"questions":[["What is wrong with the first room?",["It has only one bed","It has no window","It is in another town"],0,"The clerk notices the room has one bed."],["What does Maya do?",["Explains their needs politely","Cancels every hotel","Leaves without speaking"],0,"Maya explains the problem calmly."],["What is the final solution?",["They get a room with two beds","They sleep outside","They buy a bed"],0,"The clerk finds a suitable room."]]},
{"id":"a2-early-delivery","title":"The Early Delivery","level":"A2","tone":"#D6B17A","emoji":"📦","minutes":3,"pages":[["📦","A package for Karim arrives two days earlier than expected. He is at work when the delivery driver calls.","تصل طردة كريم قبل الموعد المتوقع بيومين. يكون في العمل عندما يتصل سائق التوصيل."],["📱","Karim checks the tracking message and asks whether the driver can leave the package with the building manager.","يتحقق كريم من رسالة التتبع ويسأل إن كان السائق يستطيع ترك الطرد لدى مسؤول المبنى."],["🏢","The driver agrees after Karim confirms the manager’s name. Karim collects the package safely that evening.","يوافق السائق بعدما يؤكد كريم اسم المسؤول. يستلم كريم الطرد بأمان في المساء."]],"vocab":{"package":["a parcel sent to someone","طرد","PAK-ij","The package arrived today."],"expected":["thought likely to happen","متوقّع","ik-SPEK-tid","The delivery was expected on Friday."],"tracking":["information showing where a parcel is","تتبّع","TRAK-ing","Use the tracking number online."],"confirm":["to check that something is correct","يؤكد","kun-FURM","Please confirm the address."]},"questions":[["Why can Karim not receive the package himself?",["He is at work","He is on a plane","He lost his phone"],0,"The driver calls while Karim is at work."],["What does Karim check?",["The tracking message","A restaurant menu","A weather map"],0,"He checks the delivery tracking message."],["Why does he confirm the manager's name?",["To make sure the package goes to the right person","To change the package color","To cancel the order"],0,"Confirming the name supports a safe handover."]]},
{"id":"a2-garden-map","title":"The Garden Map","level":"A2","tone":"#91C7A6","emoji":"🗺️","minutes":3,"pages":[["🌿","A school group visits a large public garden. Their guide gives each pair a map and a list of plants to find.","تزور مجموعة مدرسية حديقة عامة كبيرة. يعطي المرشد كل ثنائي خريطة وقائمة نباتات للعثور عليها."],["🗺️","Yasmin and Adam follow the path, but a sign points in two directions. They stop to compare the map with the sign.","تتبع ياسمين وآدم المسار، لكن لافتة تشير إلى اتجاهين. يتوقفان لمقارنة الخريطة باللافتة."],["🌻","They choose the marked eastern path and find the sunflower bed before the group meeting time.","يختاران المسار الشرقي المحدد ويصلان إلى أحواض دوار الشمس قبل موعد اجتماع المجموعة."]],"vocab":{"guide":["a person who shows visitors around","مرشد","gyd","The guide explained the garden rules."],"map":["a drawing that shows where places are","خريطة","map","The map shows the path."],"direction":["the way something points or moves","اتجاه","di-REK-shun","Which direction should we take?"],"path":["a way for people to walk","مسار","path","Follow the path to the gate."]},"questions":[["What does the guide give the students?",["A map and a plant list","A train ticket","A cooking lesson"],0,"Each pair receives a map and a list of plants."],["Why do Yasmin and Adam stop?",["The sign points in two directions","They lose their lunch","The garden closes"],0,"They stop to compare the confusing sign with the map."],["Which path do they choose?",["The marked eastern path","A path outside the garden","No path at all"],0,"They choose the marked eastern path."]]},
{"id":"b1-unsent-message","title":"The Unsent Message","level":"B1","tone":"#8CBED8","emoji":"📱","minutes":4,"pages":[["💬","After a tense team meeting, Daniel writes a message saying that his colleague ignored an important warning. He is ready to send it immediately.","بعد اجتماع متوتر، يكتب دانيال رسالة يقول فيها إن زميله تجاهل تحذيرًا مهمًا. وهو مستعد لإرسالها فورًا."],["⏸️","Before sending it, he rereads the message and realizes that he does not know whether his colleague saw the warning. He saves the draft instead.","قبل الإرسال، يعيد قراءة الرسالة ويدرك أنه لا يعرف إن كان زميله قد رأى التحذير. فيحفظ المسودة بدلًا من ذلك."],["🤝","The next morning, Daniel asks what happened. His colleague explains that the warning was buried in an old thread. They agree on a clearer alert system.","في الصباح التالي، يسأل دانيال عمّا حدث. يوضح زميله أن التحذير كان مدفونًا في محادثة قديمة. ويتفقان على نظام تنبيه أوضح."]],"vocab":{"tense":["making you feel nervous or strained","متوتر","tens","The meeting became tense."],"draft":["a version of a message not yet sent","مسودة","draft","I saved the draft before sending."],"assume":["to accept something as true without proof","يفترض","uh-SOOM","Do not assume you know what happened."],"buried":["hidden under or among other things","مدفون / مخفي","BAIR-eed","The alert was buried in a long email thread."]},"questions":[["Why does Daniel pause before sending the message?",["He realizes he lacks key information","He forgets his colleague's name","He wants to delete the project"],0,"He does not know whether his colleague saw the warning."],["Where was the warning?",["In an old message thread","On a printed poster","In a public announcement"],0,"The colleague explains that the warning was buried in an old thread."],["What do they agree to change?",["The alert system","The project goal","The office location"],0,"They agree to make alerts clearer."]]},
{"id":"b1-small-repair","title":"A Small Repair","level":"B1","tone":"#D3AA75","emoji":"🔧","minutes":4,"pages":[["🚲","Amina’s bicycle chain slips off on her way to class. She is late, but she decides not to force the pedals.","ينفلت جنزير دراجة أمينة في طريقها إلى الدرس. إنها متأخرة، لكنها تقرر ألا تضغط على الدواسات بالقوة."],["🔍","She moves to a safe place, turns the bicycle upside down, and checks how the chain sits on the gears. She remembers a repair video she watched.","تنتقل إلى مكان آمن، وتقلب الدراجة، وتفحص موضع الجنزير على التروس. وتتذكر فيديو إصلاح شاهدته."],["🚴","After carefully replacing the chain, she tests the brakes and rides slowly to a nearby workshop for a quick safety check.","بعد إعادة الجنزير بحذر، تختبر المكابح وتقود ببطء إلى ورشة قريبة لإجراء فحص سريع للسلامة."]],"vocab":{"chain":["a series of linked metal parts that moves a bicycle","جنزير","chayn","The bicycle chain came loose."],"force":["to use strength to make something move","قوة / يجبر","fors","Do not force a stuck part."],"gear":["a toothed wheel used in a machine","ترس","geer","The chain slipped off the gear."],"safety":["protection from danger or harm","سلامة","SAYF-tee","Check the brakes for safety."]},"questions":[["What does Amina avoid doing?",["Forcing the pedals","Moving to a safe place","Checking the chain"],0,"She decides not to force the pedals."],["Why does she check the gears?",["To understand how the chain fits","To clean her school bag","To find a bus ticket"],0,"She checks the chain's position on the gears."],["What does she do after repairing the chain?",["Tests the brakes and gets a safety check","Races down a hill","Throws away the bicycle"],0,"She tests the brakes and visits a workshop."]]},
{"id":"b1-shared-budget","title":"The Shared Budget","level":"B1","tone":"#A7C9A1","emoji":"🧾","minutes":4,"pages":[["💰","Four students plan a science display. They have a limited budget and each person suggests different materials.","يخطط أربعة طلاب لإعداد عرض علمي. ميزانيتهم محدودة ويقترح كل شخص مواد مختلفة."],["📋","Rather than voting immediately, Sara lists what the display must demonstrate and compares prices, quality, and reuse options.","بدل التصويت فورًا، تكتب سارة ما يجب أن يوضحه العرض وتقارن الأسعار والجودة وإمكانية إعادة الاستخدام."],["🧪","The group chooses sturdy reusable parts and borrows one tool from the laboratory. They finish the display without exceeding the budget.","تختار المجموعة أجزاء متينة قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام وتستعير أداة من المختبر. وتنهي العرض دون تجاوز الميزانية."]],"vocab":{"budget":["the amount of money available for a purpose","ميزانية","BUJ-it","We must stay within our budget."],"reuse":["to use something again","يعيد الاستخدام","ree-YOOZ","We can reuse the cardboard."],"sturdy":["strong and unlikely to break","متين","STUR-dee","The sturdy stand holds the model."],"exceed":["to go beyond a limit","يتجاوز","ik-SEED","The cost must not exceed the budget."]},"questions":[["Why does Sara make a list first?",["To identify what the display must do","To choose the most expensive item","To end the project"],0,"She defines the requirements before comparing materials."],["What factors does she compare?",["Price, quality, and reuse","Color only","The students' ages"],0,"The story lists price, quality, and reuse options."],["How does the group stay within budget?",["They reuse parts and borrow a tool","They buy every tool","They remove the science display"],0,"Reusable parts and a borrowed tool reduce costs."]]},
{"id":"b1-missing-minutes","title":"The Missing Minutes","level":"B1","tone":"#C7B2E8","emoji":"🗒️","minutes":4,"pages":[["🕒","After a club meeting, Yusuf writes a summary. Two members say that the agreed deadline is missing from his notes.","بعد اجتماع النادي، يكتب يوسف ملخصًا. يقول عضوان إن الموعد النهائي المتفق عليه غير موجود في ملاحظاته."],["📨","Yusuf checks the chat and finds two different dates. Instead of choosing one, he asks the group to confirm what was agreed.","يتحقق يوسف من المحادثة ويجد تاريخين مختلفين. وبدل اختيار أحدهما، يطلب من المجموعة تأكيد ما تم الاتفاق عليه."],["✅","The members discover that one date was a suggestion and the other was the final decision. Yusuf corrects the summary and labels future decisions clearly.","يكتشف الأعضاء أن أحد التاريخين كان اقتراحًا والآخر هو القرار النهائي. يصحح يوسف الملخص ويتفقون على تمييز القرارات المستقبلية بوضوح."]],"vocab":{"summary":["a short statement of the main points","ملخص","SUM-uh-ree","Send a summary after the meeting."],"deadline":["the latest time to finish something","موعد نهائي","DED-lyn","The deadline is next Monday."],"confirm":["to make sure something is correct","يؤكد","kun-FURM","Please confirm the final date."],"suggestion":["an idea offered for consideration","اقتراح","suh-JES-chun","That date was only a suggestion."]},"questions":[["What problem do the members notice?",["The deadline is missing","The room is too cold","The club has no name"],0,"They say the agreed deadline is missing from the notes."],["Why does Yusuf ask the group?",["Two different dates appear in the chat","He has lost the summary","He wants to cancel the meeting"],0,"The chat contains two dates, and he does not know which is final."],["What do they change for future meetings?",["They label decisions clearly","They stop writing summaries","They use fewer messages only"],0,"They agree to distinguish final decisions from suggestions."]]},
{"id":"b2-honest-estimate","title":"The Honest Estimate","level":"B2","tone":"#86C7C1","emoji":"📊","minutes":4,"pages":[["📈","A project manager asks Noor how long a software migration will take. The team has completed similar work, but this system contains unfamiliar components.","يسأل مدير المشروع نور عن المدة اللازمة لنقل نظام برمجي. أنجز الفريق أعمالًا مشابهة، لكن هذا النظام يحتوي على مكونات غير مألوفة."],["🧮","Noor gives a range rather than a single confident date. She explains which tasks are well understood and which depend on testing an old interface.","تعطي نور نطاقًا زمنيًا بدل تاريخ واحد واثق. وتشرح المهام المفهومة جيدًا وتلك التي تعتمد على اختبار واجهة قديمة."],["🤝","The team runs a short technical test, narrows the estimate, and agrees on a review point. The manager can now plan without mistaking uncertainty for failure.","يجري الفريق اختبارًا تقنيًا قصيرًا ويضيّق النطاق ويتفق على موعد للمراجعة. يستطيع المدير التخطيط دون اعتبار عدم اليقين فشلًا."]],"vocab":{"migration":["moving a system or process to a new environment","نقل نظام","my-GRAY-shun","The migration needs careful testing."],"component":["one part of a larger system","مكوّن","kum-POH-nent","This component is unfamiliar."],"range":["the space between a lower and upper value","نطاق","raynj","Give a range for the estimated time."],"uncertainty":["the state of not being fully sure","عدم يقين","un-SUR-tun-tee","The test reduces uncertainty."]},"questions":[["Why does Noor avoid giving one exact date?",["Some components are unfamiliar","The team has no experience at all","The manager did not ask"],0,"The unfamiliar components make a single confident date unreliable."],["What does the team test?",["An old interface","A new office","The manager's calendar"],0,"The estimate depends on testing an old interface."],["What is the benefit of the review point?",["The team can update the plan as evidence improves","It guarantees there will be no problems","It removes the need to communicate"],0,"A review point lets the team revise the estimate using new evidence."]]},
{"id":"b2-better-handoff","title":"A Better Handoff","level":"B2","tone":"#B4A6E4","emoji":"🔄","minutes":4,"pages":[["📂","A support team repeatedly receives incomplete reports when a shift ends. The next team spends time asking for details that should already be recorded.","يتلقى فريق الدعم تقارير ناقصة باستمرار عند انتهاء المناوبة. ويقضي الفريق التالي وقتًا في طلب تفاصيل كان ينبغي تسجيلها."],["🧩","Marek reviews several cases and notices the same gaps: current status, actions already tried, and the next owner. He proposes a short handoff template.","يراجع ماريك عدة حالات ويلاحظ الثغرات نفسها: الحالة الحالية، والإجراءات المجربة، والمسؤول التالي. يقترح نموذج تسليم مختصرًا."],["📋","After a week, the team compares response times and missing details. The template helps, but they simplify one field that staff rarely use.","بعد أسبوع، يقارن الفريق أوقات الاستجابة والتفاصيل الناقصة. يساعد النموذج، لكنهم يبسطون خانة نادرًا ما يستخدمها الموظفون."]],"vocab":{"handoff":["the transfer of responsibility or information","تسليم المسؤولية","HAND-off","A clear handoff prevents confusion."],"incomplete":["not having all the necessary parts","غير مكتمل","in-kum-PLEET","The report was incomplete."],"template":["a reusable pattern or form","نموذج","TEM-plit","Use the template for every case."],"simplify":["to make something easier to use or understand","يبسّط","SIM-pluh-fy","We should simplify the form."]},"questions":[["What problem does the team face?",["Reports lack important details","There are too many customers","The office is closing"],0,"The next team repeatedly receives incomplete reports."],["What does Marek propose?",["A short handoff template","A longer meeting every day","A new support department"],0,"He proposes a template with status, actions tried, and next owner."],["Why do they simplify a field?",["Staff rarely use it","It contains all the key information","The template is no longer needed"],0,"They review usage and simplify a field that is rarely used."]]},
{"id":"b2-quiet-customer","title":"The Quiet Customer","level":"B2","tone":"#E6B48A","emoji":"🛍️","minutes":4,"pages":[["🛒","A shop team celebrates positive reviews, yet one regular customer has stopped returning. The manager assumes the customer found a cheaper shop.","يحتفل فريق متجر بالتقييمات الإيجابية، لكن زبونًا دائمًا توقف عن العودة. يفترض المدير أن الزبون وجد متجرًا أرخص."],["👂","A staff member contacts the customer politely and asks about the experience. The customer says the new self-checkout is confusing and no one seems available to help.","يتواصل موظف مع الزبون بأدب ويسأله عن تجربته. يقول الزبون إن الدفع الذاتي الجديد مربك ولا يبدو أن أحدًا متاح للمساعدة."],["🧰","The shop adds clearer signs and schedules a staff member near the machines at busy times. The team tracks whether customers need less assistance over the next month.","يضيف المتجر لافتات أوضح ويخصص موظفًا قرب الأجهزة في أوقات الازدحام. ويتابع الفريق ما إذا كان العملاء يحتاجون مساعدة أقل خلال الشهر التالي."]],"vocab":{"regular":["happening often or on a repeated basis","منتظم / دائم","REG-yuh-ler","She is a regular customer."],"assume":["to believe something without checking","يفترض","uh-SOOM","Do not assume the reason."],"self-checkout":["a machine customers use to pay without a cashier","الدفع الذاتي","self-CHECK-out","The self-checkout was confusing."],"schedule":["to plan a time for an activity","يجدول","SKEJ-ool","They schedule staff for busy times."]},"questions":[["What does the manager first assume?",["The customer found a cheaper shop","The customer moved away","The shop is too far"],0,"The manager assumes price is the reason without checking."],["What problem does the customer describe?",["Confusing self-checkout and little help","High prices only","Poor product quality"],0,"The customer describes confusion and a lack of visible assistance."],["How will the team evaluate the changes?",["Track assistance needs over a month","Count only positive reviews","Remove all checkout machines"],0,"They plan to track whether customers need less help."]]},
{"id":"b2-data-gap","title":"The Data Gap","level":"B2","tone":"#89B7D9","emoji":"📉","minutes":4,"pages":[["📊","A school compares attendance before and after a new reminder system. The report shows fewer absences, so the team prepares to call the system a success.","تقارن مدرسة الحضور قبل نظام تذكير جديد وبعده. يُظهر التقرير انخفاض الغياب، فيستعد الفريق لاعتبار النظام ناجحًا."],["🔎","A teacher notices that the later data covers fewer school days because of a holiday. The comparison may therefore exaggerate the improvement.","تلاحظ معلمة أن البيانات اللاحقة تغطي أيامًا دراسية أقل بسبب عطلة. لذلك قد تبالغ المقارنة في تقدير التحسن."],["🧮","The team compares equivalent weeks and checks several classes separately. The improvement remains, but it is smaller than the first report suggested.","تقارن المجموعة أسابيع متكافئة وتفحص عدة صفوف كلًا على حدة. يظل التحسن موجودًا، لكنه أقل مما أوحى به التقرير الأول."]],"vocab":{"attendance":["the act of being present at a place","الحضور","uh-TEN-duns","Attendance improved this term."],"absence":["a time when someone is not present","غياب","AB-suns","The report counts each absence."],"equivalent":["equal in value, amount, or purpose","متكافئ","ih-KWIV-uh-lunt","Compare equivalent weeks."],"exaggerate":["to describe something as greater than it is","يبالغ","ig-ZAJ-uh-rayt","The first report may exaggerate the change."]},"questions":[["Why might the first report exaggerate improvement?",["The periods cover different numbers of school days","The school has no attendance data","The reminder system was never used"],0,"A holiday means the later period includes fewer school days."],["What does the team compare next?",["Equivalent weeks and separate classes","Only the first day","The price of textbooks"],0,"They compare equivalent periods and inspect classes separately."],["What is the final finding?",["Improvement remains but is smaller","Attendance becomes zero","The system is proven useless"],0,"The corrected comparison still shows improvement, but less than first reported."]]},
{"id":"c1-fragile-forecast","title":"The Fragile Forecast","level":"C1","tone":"#86BFC8","emoji":"🌦️","minutes":5,"pages":[["📈","A logistics team forecasts a sharp rise in demand using three weeks of unusually high orders. The forecast is precise, but the period may not represent normal conditions.","تتوقع مجموعة لوجستية ارتفاعًا حادًا في الطلب اعتمادًا على ثلاثة أسابيع من الطلبات المرتفعة على نحو غير معتاد. التوقع دقيق رقميًا، لكن الفترة قد لا تمثل الظروف الطبيعية."],["🔬","Ilyas traces the spike to a temporary promotion and asks the team to compare it with seasonal records, stock levels, and ordinary weeks.","يتتبع إلياس الارتفاع إلى عرض ترويجي مؤقت ويطلب مقارنة البيانات بالسجلات الموسمية ومستويات المخزون والأسابيع العادية."],["🧭","The revised model separates promotional demand from baseline demand and shows a range of plausible outcomes. Managers prepare flexible stock plans instead of committing to one brittle number.","يفصل النموذج المعدّل الطلب الناتج عن العرض الترويجي عن الطلب الأساسي ويعرض نطاقًا من النتائج المعقولة. ويعد المديرون خطط مخزون مرنة بدل الالتزام برقم واحد هش."]],"vocab":{"forecast":["a prediction based on available information","توقع","FOR-kast","The forecast uses recent sales."],"baseline":["a starting level used for comparison","مستوى أساسي","BAYS-lyn","Compare results with the baseline."],"plausible":["reasonable and likely to be true","معقول","PLAW-zuh-bul","Several outcomes are plausible."],"brittle":["easily broken or unable to adapt","هش","BRIT-ul","A brittle plan fails when conditions change."]},"questions":[["Why may the original forecast be unreliable?",["The data comes from an unusual promotion period","It contains too many seasonal records","It includes no orders at all"],0,"Three unusually high weeks may not represent ordinary demand."],["What does Ilyas compare the spike with?",["Seasonal records, stock levels, and ordinary weeks","Employee birthdays","The color of delivery trucks"],0,"He asks for several relevant comparisons to understand the spike."],["How does the revised model improve planning?",["It separates baseline and promotional demand and shows a range","It guarantees one exact outcome","It removes all uncertainty"],0,"The model represents different demand drivers and plausible outcomes."]]},
{"id":"c1-cost-convenience","title":"The Cost of Convenience","level":"C1","tone":"#D8B58A","emoji":"🛒","minutes":5,"pages":[["⚙️","A factory considers buying an automated packing line. The supplier emphasizes speed and labor savings, presenting an attractive payback estimate.","يدرس مصنع شراء خط تعبئة آلي. يركز المورد على السرعة وتوفير العمالة ويعرض تقديرًا جذابًا لفترة استرداد التكلفة."],["🧾","The operations analyst includes training, maintenance, downtime, and spare parts. The payback period grows, but the estimate now reflects costs that were previously excluded.","تضيف محللة العمليات تكاليف التدريب والصيانة والتوقف وقطع الغيار. تطول فترة الاسترداد، لكن التقدير يعكس الآن تكاليف كانت مستبعدة."],["🏭","The team runs a pilot on one shift and records both output and interruptions. They postpone a full purchase until the pilot shows whether the convenience creates value under real conditions.","يجري الفريق تجربة على مناوبة واحدة ويسجل الإنتاج والانقطاعات. ويؤجل الشراء الكامل حتى تكشف التجربة إن كانت سهولة التشغيل تحقق قيمة في الظروف الواقعية."]],"vocab":{"payback":["the time needed for an investment to recover its cost","فترة استرداد التكلفة","PAY-bak","The payback period is three years."],"downtime":["time when equipment is not operating","وقت التوقف","DOWN-tym","Maintenance can reduce downtime."],"exclude":["to leave something out","يستبعد","ik-SKLOOD","The first estimate excluded training."],"pilot":["a small test before wider use","تجربة أولية","PY-lut","The factory ran a pilot first."]},"questions":[["What does the supplier emphasize?",["Speed and labor savings","Training failures","Spare-part shortages"],0,"The supplier highlights speed and labor savings."],["Why does the payback period grow?",["The analyst adds previously excluded costs","The line becomes faster","The factory stops recording costs"],0,"Including training, maintenance, downtime, and spare parts raises the estimate."],["Why run a pilot before buying the full line?",["To test value under real operating conditions","To avoid collecting any data","To guarantee zero interruptions"],0,"A pilot checks actual output and interruptions before a large commitment."]]},
{"id":"c1-question-credit","title":"A Question of Credit","level":"C1","tone":"#B8A9DE","emoji":"📝","minutes":5,"pages":[["🏆","A project presentation praises the team lead for an improvement developed largely by a junior engineer, Salma. Salma says nothing during the meeting.","يشيد عرض مشروع بقائد الفريق بسبب تحسين طوّره إلى حد كبير مهندس مبتدئ يُدعى سلمى. لا تقول سلمى شيئًا أثناء الاجتماع."],["🤔","The lead notices her silence and later asks whether the presentation represented the work fairly. Salma explains which tests and design changes she carried out.","يلاحظ القائد صمتها ويسألها لاحقًا إن كان العرض قد مثّل العمل بإنصاف. تشرح سلمى الاختبارات والتغييرات التصميمية التي نفذتها."],["🤝","The lead corrects the project record, credits Salma’s contribution, and agrees to identify responsibilities more clearly in future reviews. The correction improves both recognition and accountability.","يصحح القائد سجل المشروع وينسب مساهمة سلمى إليها ويتفق على تحديد المسؤوليات بوضوح أكبر في المراجعات القادمة. يعزز التصحيح التقدير والمساءلة معًا."]],"vocab":{"contribution":["something a person adds to a shared result","مساهمة","kon-truh-BYOO-shun","Her contribution improved the design."],"represent":["to describe or show something accurately","يمثل","rep-ri-ZENT","The report should represent the work fairly."],"credit":["recognition for someone's work or achievement","تقدير / نسبة الفضل","KRED-it","Give credit to the person who did the work."],"accountability":["responsibility for actions and results","مساءلة","uh-kown-tuh-BIL-uh-tee","Clear roles improve accountability."]},"questions":[["Why does the lead speak to Salma afterward?",["He notices her silence and checks whether the work was represented fairly","He wants her to leave the team","He has lost the presentation"],0,"He asks whether the presentation represented the work fairly."],["What does Salma explain?",["The tests and design changes she carried out","The team's lunch plans","A new office policy"],0,"She describes her own technical contributions."],["What changes after the conversation?",["The record is corrected and responsibilities will be clearer","The project is cancelled","The team stops reviewing work"],0,"The lead corrects the record and agrees on clearer attribution."]]},
{"id":"c1-delayed-warning","title":"The Delayed Warning","level":"C1","tone":"#D8A36F","emoji":"⚡","minutes":5,"pages":[["⚠️","A maintenance dashboard shows a rising vibration trend on a pump. The alert threshold has not been crossed, so the shift team continues operating normally.","تعرض لوحة الصيانة ارتفاعًا تدريجيًا في اهتزاز مضخة. لم يتم تجاوز عتبة الإنذار، لذا يواصل فريق المناوبة التشغيل بشكل طبيعي."],["📉","An engineer compares the trend with previous failures and notices that the current rate of change is unusual. She records the evidence and requests an inspection before the threshold is reached.","يقارن مهندس الاتجاه بأعطال سابقة ويلاحظ أن معدل التغير الحالي غير معتاد. يسجل الأدلة ويطلب فحصًا قبل بلوغ العتبة."],["🛠️","Inspection finds a loose mounting that could have caused damage if left unchecked. The team reviews the alert policy so it considers trend and context, not only a fixed limit.","يكشف الفحص عن تثبيت مرتخٍ كان قد يسبب ضررًا إن تُرك دون معالجة. يراجع الفريق سياسة الإنذار لتراعي الاتجاه والسياق، لا حدًا ثابتًا فقط."]],"vocab":{"threshold":["a level at which an action or change begins","عتبة","THRESH-hold","The alert threshold was not reached."],"trend":["the general direction of change over time","اتجاه","trend","The trend shows rising vibration."],"inspection":["a careful examination","فحص","in-SPEK-shun","The pump needs an inspection."],"context":["the conditions that help explain a fact","سياق","KON-tekst","Context helps explain the measurement."]},"questions":[["Why does the engineer request an inspection early?",["The rate of change is unusual","The pump has already stopped","The threshold is set to zero"],0,"The trend looks unusual compared with previous failures."],["What does the inspection find?",["A loose mounting","An empty fuel tank","A broken display screen"],0,"The inspection identifies a loose mounting."],["What policy change does the team consider?",["Include trend and context in alerts","Remove every alarm","Ignore measurements until a failure"],0,"The team reviews a policy based only on a fixed threshold."]]},
{"id":"c2-metric-mattered","title":"The Metric That Mattered","level":"C2","tone":"#8FBFC4","emoji":"📐","minutes":5,"pages":[["📊","A public service department reports that average waiting time has fallen. Senior leaders celebrate, although complaints about the service have increased.","يعلن قسم خدمة عامة أن متوسط وقت الانتظار انخفض. يحتفل المسؤولون رغم زيادة الشكاوى بشأن الخدمة."],["🔍","An analyst separates routine enquiries from complex cases and finds that the new queue prioritizes short interactions. The average improved partly because the case mix changed, while difficult cases waited longer.","تفصل محللة الاستفسارات الروتينية عن الحالات المعقدة وتكتشف أن الطابور الجديد يعطي الأولوية للتفاعلات القصيرة. تحسن المتوسط جزئيًا بسبب تغير نوع الحالات، بينما انتظرت الحالات الصعبة مدة أطول."],["🧭","The department reports waiting times by case type, alongside completion quality and repeat visits. Leaders revise the target so staff cannot improve the headline metric by neglecting complex users.","يعرض القسم أوقات الانتظار حسب نوع الحالة، إلى جانب جودة الإنجاز والزيارات المتكررة. ويعدل المسؤولون الهدف حتى لا يحسّن الموظفون الرقم الرئيسي على حساب أصحاب الحالات المعقدة."]],"vocab":{"aggregate":["a value formed by combining many individual values","قيمة إجمالية","AG-ri-git","An aggregate average can hide differences."],"case-mix":["the types of cases included in a group of data","تركيبة الحالات","KAYS-miks","A changed case mix affects the average."],"prioritize":["to give something greater importance","يعطي الأولوية","pry-OR-uh-tyze","The queue prioritizes short requests."],"perverse":["having an effect opposite to the intended one","عكسي / غير مرغوب","per-VURS","A poorly designed target can create perverse incentives."]},"questions":[["Why did the average waiting time fall?",["The queue prioritized short interactions and the case mix changed","Every complex case was solved immediately","The department stopped measuring time"],0,"The analyst finds that shorter interactions were prioritized and the mix of cases changed."],["Why are complaints still increasing?",["Complex cases wait longer despite the improved average","There are no complex cases","The average is always meaningless"],0,"The headline average hides longer waits for difficult cases."],["What is the purpose of reporting several measures?",["To reduce the chance of optimizing one metric at users' expense","To make the report longer without reason","To remove accountability"],0,"Case-specific times and quality measures give a more balanced picture."]]},
{"id":"c2-consensus-pressure","title":"A Consensus Under Pressure","level":"C2","tone":"#B5A6D9","emoji":"🏛️","minutes":5,"pages":[["🗳️","A committee must approve a major timetable by the end of the day. The chair asks for objections, but no one speaks. The minutes record unanimous agreement.","يجب على لجنة اعتماد جدول زمني مهم قبل نهاية اليوم. يطلب الرئيس الاعتراضات، لكن لا يتحدث أحد. ويسجل المحضر موافقة بالإجماع."],["🧩","A junior member later tells the facilitator that several people privately doubt the assumptions but fear being seen as obstructive. The silence reflected the room’s hierarchy more than shared confidence.","يخبر عضو مبتدئ الميسّر لاحقًا أن عدة أشخاص يشككون سرًا في الافتراضات لكنهم يخشون الظهور بمظهر المعطّل. عكس الصمت تراتبية الغرفة أكثر مما عكس ثقة مشتركة."],["🗣️","The facilitator reopens the discussion with anonymous risk statements and asks the committee to distinguish unresolved concerns from acceptable trade-offs. The final decision is slower but better informed.","يعيد الميسّر فتح النقاش عبر إفادات مجهولة عن المخاطر ويطلب من اللجنة التمييز بين المخاوف غير المحسومة والمفاضلات المقبولة. يصبح القرار النهائي أبطأ لكنه أكثر استنارة."]],"vocab":{"unanimous":["in agreement by everyone","بالإجماع","yoo-NAN-uh-mus","The minutes recorded unanimous agreement."],"hierarchy":["a system of ranks or levels of authority","تراتبية","HY-uh-rar-kee","Hierarchy can affect who speaks."],"obstructive":["making progress difficult on purpose or in effect","معطّل","ub-STRUK-tiv","They feared being called obstructive."],"trade-off":["a situation where one benefit requires giving up another","مفاضلة","TRAYD-off","The committee discussed the trade-off."]},"questions":[["What does the silence initially appear to mean?",["Unanimous agreement","A cancelled meeting","A technical failure"],0,"The minutes record unanimous agreement because no one objects."],["What does the junior member reveal?",["Some members doubt assumptions but fear speaking","Everyone fully supports the timetable","The committee has no deadline"],0,"Several people privately doubt the assumptions and fear appearing obstructive."],["Why use anonymous risk statements?",["To surface concerns that hierarchy may suppress","To remove the need for evidence","To guarantee everyone agrees"],0,"Anonymous statements can make it safer to raise concerns under social pressure."]]},
{"id":"c2-ambiguous-promise","title":"The Ambiguous Promise","level":"C2","tone":"#D6AA83","emoji":"🗣️","minutes":5,"pages":[["📄","A director tells a partner, “We should be able to deliver the revised system by June.” The partner records June as a firm commitment and schedules a public launch.","يقول مدير لشريك: «ينبغي أن نتمكن من تسليم النظام المعدّل بحلول يونيو». يسجل الشريك يونيو باعتباره التزامًا مؤكدًا ويحدد موعد إطلاق عام."],["🔎","When the team later explains that testing could extend the timeline, both sides feel misled. The director intended a conditional forecast; the partner heard a promise.","عندما يوضح الفريق لاحقًا أن الاختبارات قد تمدد الجدول، يشعر الطرفان بأنهما تعرضا للتضليل. قصد المدير توقعًا مشروطًا، بينما فهم الشريك وعدًا."],["🤝","They revisit the wording and separate the target date from the decision criteria: June remains the goal if reliability tests pass by a stated checkpoint. Each side confirms the same interpretation in writing.","يعيدان صياغة العبارة ويفصلان التاريخ المستهدف عن معايير القرار: يظل يونيو هدفًا إذا اجتازت اختبارات الاعتمادية نقطة تحقق محددة. ويؤكد كل طرف الفهم نفسه كتابةً."]],"vocab":{"conditional":["depending on something else being true","مشروط","kun-DISH-uh-nul","The date is conditional on test results."],"commitment":["a promise or firm obligation","التزام","kuh-MIT-ment","The partner understood it as a commitment."],"interpretation":["the meaning someone understands from a statement","تفسير","in-tur-pruh-TAY-shun","Their interpretations were different."],"checkpoint":["a planned moment to review progress or evidence","نقطة تحقق","CHECK-point","The team set a checkpoint in May."]},"questions":[["Why do the two sides disagree about June?",["They interpret a conditional forecast differently","The system has already launched","The partner changes the month"],0,"The director intends a conditional forecast while the partner hears a firm promise."],["What risk does the misunderstanding create?",["The partner schedules a public launch too early","The team stops testing completely","The deadline disappears from the calendar"],0,"The partner treats June as guaranteed and schedules a launch."],["How do they reduce future ambiguity?",["Separate the target from conditions and confirm it in writing","Avoid discussing dates ever again","Let each side keep its own interpretation"],0,"They define a goal, a test condition, and a checkpoint, then confirm the shared meaning."]]},
{"id":"c2-missing-counterfactual","title":"The Missing Counterfactual","level":"C2","tone":"#9DB8E0","emoji":"🧠","minutes":5,"pages":[["📈","A city introduces a new traffic signal pattern. Travel time falls by eight percent in the following month, and the report attributes the entire improvement to the change.","تطبق مدينة نمطًا جديدًا لإشارات المرور. ينخفض زمن الرحلة بنسبة ثمانية بالمئة في الشهر التالي، وينسب التقرير التحسن كله إلى التغيير."],["🔬","An evaluator notes that roadworks also ended during that month and school holidays altered traffic. Without a comparison, the observed change cannot isolate the signal pattern’s effect.","يلاحظ مقيّم أن أعمال الطرق انتهت أيضًا خلال ذلك الشهر وأن العطلات المدرسية غيّرت حركة المرور. من دون مقارنة، لا يمكن عزل أثر نمط الإشارات عن بقية العوامل."],["🧭","The city compares similar corridors and historical periods, while acknowledging remaining limitations. The signal pattern appears to help, but the report narrows its claim and recommends continued monitoring.","تقارن المدينة ممرات مرورية مشابهة وفترات تاريخية مع الإقرار بالقيود المتبقية. يبدو أن نمط الإشارات مفيد، لكن التقرير يضيّق ادعاءه ويوصي بمواصلة المراقبة."]],"vocab":{"attribute":["to say that something was caused by a person or thing","ينسب","uh-TRIB-yoot","The report attributes the change to the new plan."],"counterfactual":["a comparison with what might have happened otherwise","حالة افتراضية مضادة","kown-ter-FAK-choo-ul","A counterfactual helps assess what would happen without the intervention."],"isolate":["to identify one factor separately from others","يعزل","EYE-suh-layt","The comparison tries to isolate the effect."],"limitation":["a condition that restricts what can be concluded","قيد","lim-ih-TAY-shun","The report explains its limitations."]},"questions":[["Why is the original causal claim weak?",["Other changes happened at the same time","Travel time increased in every period","The signal pattern was never changed"],0,"Roadworks ended and school holidays altered traffic during the same month."],["What does a comparison help the evaluator do?",["Separate the signal effect from other factors","Prove every result with certainty","Ignore historical information"],0,"Comparable corridors and periods help assess the intervention more carefully."],["How does the final report change?",["It narrows the claim and recommends monitoring","It claims absolute proof","It removes all mention of limitations"],0,"The report acknowledges limits while saying the signal pattern appears to help."]]}];

const STORY_DECISIONS = {"a1-lost-key":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"What should Mia do next?","options":[{"text":"Ask someone for help.","response":"Asking for help can be useful when you are stuck."},{"text":"Look carefully in one more place.","response":"Good thinking: checking carefully may solve the problem."},{"text":"Give up and leave.","response":"Sometimes a short pause helps, but giving up too early can miss a solution."}]},"a1-rainy-picnic":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"The rain starts. What is the best plan?","options":[{"text":"Find a dry place and keep the picnic.","response":"A flexible plan lets Sam and his sister enjoy the day."},{"text":"Leave the food in the rain.","response":"Food can get wet, so protecting it is a practical first step."},{"text":"Wait outside until the rain stops.","response":"Waiting is possible, but a nearby shelter may be more comfortable."}]},"a2-night-train":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"How can Nora help the man?","options":[{"text":"Ask where he last saw the suitcase.","response":"A clear question helps narrow down where to look."},{"text":"Tell him to buy another suitcase.","response":"Replacing something is costly; checking the facts first is wiser."},{"text":"Ignore him because the train is late.","response":"A small act of help can make a difficult wait easier."}]},"a2-bread-mystery":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"Leo wants to find out what happened. What should he do?","options":[{"text":"Watch quietly before blaming anyone.","response":"Observing first helps Leo avoid accusing the wrong person."},{"text":"Accuse his brother again.","response":"Blaming someone without evidence can hurt trust."},{"text":"Hide all the food forever.","response":"Protecting the bread may help, but it will not explain the mystery."}]},"b1-last-bus":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"Would you take the cyclist’s advice?","options":[{"text":"Check the route and try it.","response":"Checking a suggestion, then acting quickly, balances caution and initiative."},{"text":"Call a taxi without listening.","response":"A taxi is an option, but it may cost more than necessary."},{"text":"Stay at the same stop.","response":"Waiting may not help if the last bus has already left."}]},"b1-quiet-lab":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"What should the team test first?","options":[{"text":"Close the window and repeat the measurement.","response":"Changing one variable at a time is a useful way to test a cause."},{"text":"Replace every sensor immediately.","response":"Replacing equipment before testing can waste time and money."},{"text":"Ignore the strange readings.","response":"Unexpected results are clues worth investigating."}]},"b2-open-door":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"How should the manager respond to blunt feedback?","options":[{"text":"Listen and look for a pattern.","response":"Listening for recurring concerns can reveal the real bottleneck."},{"text":"Defend every decision immediately.","response":"Defensiveness can discourage people from speaking honestly."},{"text":"Cancel all future meetings.","response":"The problem is not necessarily meetings, but how decisions are made."}]},"b2-second-chance":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"What would help Rafi improve?","options":[{"text":"Review the recording and practise in small steps.","response":"Specific feedback and steady practice make improvement manageable."},{"text":"Avoid speaking in public again.","response":"Avoidance may reduce anxiety briefly but limits practice."},{"text":"Pretend the speech went perfectly.","response":"Honest reflection gives Rafi something useful to improve."}]},"c1-quiet-objection":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"The team is uncomfortable with Leila’s question. What should she do next?","options":[{"text":"Ask for the evidence behind the estimates and invite the team to review it together.","response":"This keeps the discussion focused on evidence, gives colleagues a shared problem to solve, and avoids turning the question into a personal confrontation."},{"text":"Withdraw the concern so the meeting can finish on time.","response":"This may preserve short-term comfort, but the uncertainty remains hidden and the team loses a chance to reduce the risk."},{"text":"Insist that the schedule is wrong before checking the records.","response":"Raising a risk matters, but declaring the plan wrong before checking evidence can weaken trust and make a useful concern easier to dismiss."}]},"c1-cost-of-clarity":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A report claims a process is faster but leaves out maintenance. What do you ask?","options":[{"text":"What costs or trade-offs are missing?","response":"Asking about trade-offs makes the comparison more useful."},{"text":"Can we remove the limitations section?","response":"Removing limitations makes a report less reliable."},{"text":"Is the report longer than before?","response":"Length alone does not tell us whether the evidence is complete."}]},"c2-language-of-consensus":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A committee seems unanimous, but several people are silent. What should the chair do?","options":[{"text":"Invite objections before confirming the decision.","response":"Inviting dissent helps distinguish genuine consensus from acquiescence."},{"text":"Treat silence as full agreement.","response":"Silence may reflect pressure rather than genuine agreement."},{"text":"End the meeting immediately.","response":"A short invitation to disagree may uncover important risks."}]},"c2-unintended-inference":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A colleague calls your plan “ambitious.” How do you clarify the meaning?","options":[{"text":"Ask which milestones need stronger evidence.","response":"A specific question turns an ambiguous comment into actionable feedback."},{"text":"Assume they are insulting the plan.","response":"The word can signal praise or doubt; context matters."},{"text":"Ignore the comment entirely.","response":"Clarifying the concern can prevent misunderstandings later."}]},
"a1-blue-umbrella":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The man is getting wet. What can Ana do?","options":[{"text":"Share her umbrella.","response":"Sharing gives both people some protection from the rain."},{"text":"Laugh and walk away.","response":"That would leave someone who needs help in the rain."},{"text":"Hide her umbrella.","response":"Keeping it to herself would not help the man."}]},
"a1-helpful-neighbor":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"Ben's bucket is broken. What should he do?","options":[{"text":"Ask a neighbor for help.","response":"Asking politely can help solve a simple problem."},{"text":"Leave the flowers without water forever.","response":"The flowers still need water, so the problem remains."},{"text":"Throw away all the flowers.","response":"That is not necessary when the problem is the bucket."}]},
"a1-wrong-lunchbox":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The food in the box is not Lina's. What should she do?","options":[{"text":"Check the name on the box.","response":"Checking the name helps her find the right owner."},{"text":"Eat everything quickly.","response":"The food may belong to another student."},{"text":"Hide the lunchbox.","response":"Hiding it will not help either student find their food."}]},
"a1-note-grandma":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"Tom has written a note. What should he do next?","options":[{"text":"Take it to Grandma.","response":"Taking the note to her lets her read his message."},{"text":"Throw it into the river.","response":"Then Grandma will not receive the message."},{"text":"Forget the visit.","response":"He wants to see Grandma, so he can continue with his plan."}]},
"a2-library-card":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"Nora has never used the library. What is a good first step?","options":[{"text":"Ask the librarian how to register.","response":"The librarian can explain the process and required information."},{"text":"Take a book without telling anyone.","response":"Books must be checked out so the library can track them."},{"text":"Leave without asking a question.","response":"She would miss the help that makes borrowing straightforward."}]},
"a2-room-for-two":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The room does not match their needs. What should Maya do?","options":[{"text":"Explain the problem politely.","response":"A clear, respectful explanation helps the clerk find a solution."},{"text":"Shout before checking the booking.","response":"Anger may make the conversation harder without adding useful information."},{"text":"Say nothing and accept it.","response":"The mismatch may be fixable if the hotel knows about it."}]},
"a2-early-delivery":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"Karim is at work when the driver calls. What should he do?","options":[{"text":"Arrange a safe handover with a trusted person.","response":"A confirmed handover gives the driver a clear and safer option."},{"text":"Tell the driver to leave it anywhere.","response":"An unattended package could be lost or taken."},{"text":"Share his account password.","response":"A delivery does not require sharing a private password."}]},
"a2-garden-map":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The sign seems confusing. What should they do?","options":[{"text":"Compare the sign with the map.","response":"Using two sources helps them make a more informed choice."},{"text":"Run in a random direction.","response":"Moving without checking may take them farther from the group."},{"text":"Throw the map away.","response":"The map is useful information they should keep."}]},
"b1-unsent-message":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"Daniel is angry but is not sure what happened. What is the best next step?","options":[{"text":"Pause and check the facts first.","response":"A short pause can prevent an accusation based on an untested assumption."},{"text":"Send the harshest version immediately.","response":"An immediate accusation may damage trust before the facts are clear."},{"text":"Tell the whole team the colleague is careless.","response":"Public blame spreads an unverified conclusion instead of solving the communication problem."}]},
"b1-small-repair":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The chain slips off while Amina is late. What matters most first?","options":[{"text":"Move somewhere safe and inspect the problem.","response":"Safety comes before speed, and inspection helps avoid further damage."},{"text":"Pedal harder until it works.","response":"Forcing the pedals could damage the bicycle or cause a fall."},{"text":"Ride into traffic to save time.","response":"That increases risk instead of solving the mechanical problem."}]},
"b1-shared-budget":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The group has different ideas and little money. What should they do first?","options":[{"text":"Agree on the requirements and compare options.","response":"Shared requirements make comparisons fairer and keep the group focused."},{"text":"Let the loudest person decide everything.","response":"That may ignore important needs and useful alternatives."},{"text":"Buy materials before checking prices.","response":"Buying first risks spending the limited budget too quickly."}]},
"b1-missing-minutes":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The chat contains two possible dates. What should Yusuf do?","options":[{"text":"Ask the group to confirm the final decision.","response":"Confirmation prevents a guess from becoming an incorrect record."},{"text":"Choose the date he likes best.","response":"Personal preference does not establish what the group agreed."},{"text":"Delete both dates without asking.","response":"Removing information would leave the uncertainty unresolved."}]},
"b2-honest-estimate":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The manager wants one date, but key tasks remain uncertain. How should Noor respond?","options":[{"text":"Explain a realistic range and what evidence would narrow it.","response":"A transparent range supports planning while making uncertainty and next steps explicit."},{"text":"Promise the earliest date to sound confident.","response":"An unsupported promise can create avoidable pressure and damage trust."},{"text":"Refuse to estimate anything.","response":"A useful range is possible even when the exact duration is unknown."}]},
"b2-better-handoff":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The same information is missing from many handoffs. What is the best response?","options":[{"text":"Find the recurring gaps and design a simple template.","response":"A shared structure addresses the repeated cause while keeping the process practical."},{"text":"Blame each person separately without changing the process.","response":"Individual reminders may not fix a recurring system-level gap."},{"text":"Require a long report for every small case.","response":"Excessive documentation can add friction without guaranteeing useful information."}]},
"b2-quiet-customer":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A regular customer stops visiting, but the reason is unknown. What should the team do?","options":[{"text":"Ask respectfully and listen before deciding.","response":"Direct feedback tests the assumption and may reveal a fixable experience problem."},{"text":"Assume price is the only cause.","response":"An untested assumption may lead to the wrong solution."},{"text":"Ignore the change because other reviews are positive.","response":"Positive feedback does not explain why this particular customer left."}]},
"b2-data-gap":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The data looks positive, but the periods are not comparable. What should the team do?","options":[{"text":"Correct the comparison before making a claim.","response":"Comparable periods help separate a real effect from a measurement difference."},{"text":"Publish the strongest number immediately.","response":"That risks overstating the evidence and weakening trust."},{"text":"Discard all the data without review.","response":"The data may still be useful once the comparison is made fairly."}]},
"c1-fragile-forecast":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A precise forecast relies on a short, unusual period. What is the strongest response?","options":[{"text":"Test whether the period represents normal conditions.","response":"Precision is not the same as reliability; representative data matters."},{"text":"Treat the number as certain because it has decimals.","response":"Extra decimal places cannot correct biased or unrepresentative data."},{"text":"Ignore every recent order.","response":"Recent data is useful, but it needs context rather than automatic rejection."}]},
"c1-cost-convenience":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A proposal looks attractive but excludes recurring costs. What should the team do?","options":[{"text":"Include the full lifecycle costs and test key assumptions.","response":"A complete cost model and a pilot give a more credible basis for investment."},{"text":"Approve it because the initial estimate is simple.","response":"Simplicity does not compensate for missing costs that may change the decision."},{"text":"Reject automation without examining the evidence.","response":"The omitted costs matter, but the technology may still be worthwhile after a fair assessment."}]},
"c1-question-credit":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A presentation may have overlooked a colleague's contribution. What is a constructive response?","options":[{"text":"Check the record and correct attribution with specific evidence.","response":"Specific evidence allows recognition to be corrected without relying on vague accusation."},{"text":"Assume the omission was deliberate and accuse the lead publicly.","response":"Intent is not yet established; a factual conversation is more likely to repair the record."},{"text":"Ignore it because the project succeeded.","response":"A successful outcome does not remove the need for fair recognition and accountability."}]},
"c1-delayed-warning":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A warning threshold has not been crossed, but the trend looks unusual. What should the engineer do?","options":[{"text":"Document the trend and assess the risk in context.","response":"A trend can reveal emerging risk before a fixed threshold is crossed."},{"text":"Ignore it because the alarm is still quiet.","response":"A threshold is useful, but it may not capture every developing failure."},{"text":"Declare that failure is certain.","response":"An unusual trend justifies investigation, not an unsupported certainty."}]},
"c2-metric-mattered":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A headline metric improves while complaints rise. What should the analyst investigate?","options":[{"text":"Check subgroup results and whether incentives changed behavior.","response":"Disaggregated data can expose trade-offs hidden by an aggregate metric and reveal unintended incentives."},{"text":"Declare the service successful based on the average alone.","response":"A single aggregate measure cannot explain the rise in complaints."},{"text":"Stop collecting complaint data.","response":"Removing a conflicting signal conceals the problem rather than resolving it."}]},
"c2-consensus-pressure":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A committee is silent under time pressure. Can silence safely be treated as consensus?","options":[{"text":"Invite concerns through a safer, structured process.","response":"Structured dissent helps distinguish genuine agreement from silence caused by status or fear."},{"text":"Record agreement immediately because no one objected.","response":"Silence is ambiguous, especially when hierarchy or deadlines make dissent costly."},{"text":"Assume every member secretly opposes the plan.","response":"That overcorrects in the other direction; concerns should be elicited rather than presumed."}]},
"c2-ambiguous-promise":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A partner treats a qualified forecast as a firm promise. What should the director clarify?","options":[{"text":"State the target, conditions, and checkpoint explicitly.","response":"Separating an aspiration from its conditions makes expectations testable and reduces interpretive risk."},{"text":"Insist the partner should have guessed the intended meaning.","response":"When wording permits two plausible readings, relying on inference leaves the mismatch unresolved."},{"text":"Remove all dates from future discussions.","response":"Avoiding dates sacrifices useful planning rather than making commitments clearer."}]},
"c2-missing-counterfactual":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"An outcome improves after a policy change, but other factors changed too. What conclusion is justified?","options":[{"text":"Compare plausible alternatives and qualify the causal claim.","response":"A counterfactual comparison helps estimate the intervention’s contribution without overstating certainty."},{"text":"Attribute the entire improvement to the policy.","response":"Timing alone does not establish causation when other changes coincide."},{"text":"Conclude the policy had no effect at all.","response":"Confounding factors limit certainty; they do not automatically prove the intervention had no effect."}]}
}
for (const story of STORIES) { if (STORY_DECISIONS[story.id]) story.decision = STORY_DECISIONS[story.id]; }
for (const s of STORIES) { s.pages=s.pages.map(([scene,text,ar])=>({scene,text,ar})); s.questions=s.questions.map(([q,answers,correct,explain])=>({q,sub:'Choose the best answer.',answers,correct,explain})); const vocab={}; for(const [k,v] of Object.entries(s.vocab))vocab[k]={meaning:v[0],ar:v[1],pronunciation:v[2],example:v[3]};s.vocab=vocab; }